func=jag::PacketHandlers::ChangeLobby	func_addr=0x0017e330	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt op212 SET_WORLD_TARGET handler. Wire: [gStr host (CP1252, NUL-terminated)] [g2 worldId] [g2 port1] [g2 port2]. Builds WorldLobbyData{worldId,host@+0x10,port1@+0x28,port2@+0x2a,isWorld/+0x2c\e1} and stores it in WorldSwitcher (client+RELA[0xd01]) at +0x28(shared_ptr)/+0x30(raw) \e the LOBBY-node slot. CRITICAL: the +0x30 slot is consumed ONLY by LOBBY logins (loginType!\e2) in LoginStepWaitingConnectionOpened; it does NOT set the WORLD target (+0x20) and does NOT trigger any login. Sending op212 to retarget the WORLD is a no-op for world login. Field order (host FIRST) DIFFERS from op213. RE rs2client.948-5.
