func=jag::PacketHandlers::SetTarget	func_addr=0x000ee450	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eSET_TARGET direction\eSERVER opcode\e155 size\e3\n\nASSIGNED BY ELIMINATION -- lower confidence than the rest of this bucket. The other twelve size-3\nhandlers were each positively proven, and SET_TARGET was the only official name left; the counts\nare equal (13 handlers / 13 names).\n\nPayload: 3-byte little-endian value (b0 | b1<<8 | b2<<16) written to loggedInPlayer+0x98, guarded\nby a null check on the object pointer (Client+0x19b30).\nSupporting evidence: Client+0x19b30 is the logged-in-player / ClientState object identified by the\nconfirmed JCOINS_UPDATE  (+0x40) and LOYALTY_UPDATE  (+0x44); its\nneighbouring server-settable fields are combat/interaction state -- +0xa0 (op) and\n+0xa4 \e REDUCE_NPC_ATTACK_PRIORITY . A 24-bit target handle fits that neighbourhood.\nNOT independently proven: no consumer of +0x98 was located. Re-verify before relying on it.
func=jag::LoginManager::StartWorldLogin	func_addr=0x001afb00	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::LoginManager::StartWorldLogin - begins the WORLD login (loginType\e2). Pulls the game-connection ClientStream shared_ptr from ConnectionManager+0x10/+0x18 (the GAME slot, distinct from the lobby/login slot at CM+0x28), reuses the lobby-login credentials/token strings at LoginMgr+0x70/+0x88, then calls StartLogin(type\e2,...). StartLogin -> login sub-state 10 -> LoginStepWaitingConnectionOpened opens a NEW socket to WorldSwitcher+0x20 (committed world target) host:port, then runs the standard NXT login handshake (CreateLoginRSAPacket: RSA-wrapped block) over that fresh socket. Triggered by (a) OnMainStateTransition on state 0x25 (set by SWITCH_WORLD op213), or (b) the lobby 'play' CS2 opcode FUN_002dc380 once the world target is already committed. RE rs2client.948-5.
func=jag::Js5ResourceProvider::WorkerOnMessage	func_addr=0x00986710	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Js5 worker message dispatch. case 10 \e accept master index (255/255) -> builds this->masterIndex (this+0x25b8) whose archive_count gates all reftable requests. case 0x14 \e deliver index/reftable to disk cache. case 0x1e \e provide group. case 0x28 \e compare/verify master index.\nARCHIVE CAPACITY \e 67 (hardcoded): case 10 zeroes 0x43\e67 per-archive state entries (this+0x25d0); per-archive Js5Index arrays at this+0x26e0/+0x6bf8/+0xb110 are each 67*0x108 (ending at this+0xf628). archiveId directly indexes these 67-slot arrays (no per-array bound), so requestable archiveId is 0..66. Therefore master-index archive_count byte MUST be >\e 67 to avoid the RequestGroupFromDisk/SendIndex assert (archiveId < archive_count).
func=jag::Js5ResourceProvider::WorkerOnMessage	func_addr=0x00986710	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=1146	cu_index_from_entry=217	text=case 10 (accept master index 255/255): parse received blob into a Js5MasterIndex (alloc 0x20) and store at this+0x25b8. Js5MasterIndex.archive_count(+0x10) \e the single archive-count byte in the blob. THIS is the value RequestGroupFromDisk / SendIndex bounds-check archiveId against. Later in this case the per-archive disk group-status array (diskCache+0x10198+archiveId*0x20) is (re)sized to masterIndexEntry.file_count+1.
