func=jag::input::Input::OnKeyDownInner	func_addr=0x00cb3920	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::input::Input::OnKeyDownInner(Input *this, int keycode) - EXACTLY TWO PARAMETERS (prologue reads only RDI and ESI; RDX/RCX are never touched).\nDispatch order: for each node of this->namedHandlers (rbtree, in key order) take handler \e *(node+0x38) and call every std::function in handler->onKeyDown (+0x208, lock +0x220); then the same for this->globalHandler (+0x08). A listener returning true CONSUMES the event and stops dispatch.\nIMPORTANT ORDERING: InputState's key-down flag for this keycode is set to 1 ONLY AFTER all dispatch completes. A listener that calls InputState::IsKeyDown(keycode) during its own key-down therefore sees the OLD (false) value. Modifier state for a synthetic sequence must be established by a PRIOR OnKeyDown call, not the same one.\nthis->mLock (+0x18) is a RECURSIVE pthread mutex, so re-entering from inside a listener on the same thread is safe.
