func=jag::HitmarksAndHeadbars::AddHeadbar	func_addr=0x00491e50	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::HitmarksAndHeadbars::AddHeadbar (949-1)\n\nvoid AddHeadbar(HitmarksAndHeadbars* ring, PathingEntity* owner,\n                int type1, int type2, uint startCycle,\n                int bar1FromFill, int bar1ToFill,\n                int bar2FromFill, int bar2ToFill, int transitionCycles)\n\ntype1/type2 \e headbar def ids from CONFIG GROUP 72 (registry index DAT_016929c0\n\e 0x48, set by ConfigProvider::RegisterConfigGroupIds; consumed at\nConfigProvider::EnsureTypeListsLoaded slot +0x150). NOT config group 46 --\ngroup 46 is the type decoded by FUN_0056d5f0 (currently mislabelled\njag::game::HeadbarType::DecodeType). type2 < 0 \e no second bar; an invalid def\nfor either id aborts the call.\n\nstartCycle \e the cycle at which this bar state ACTIVATES (caller passes\ncurrentCycle + wireDelay). It is NOT an end cycle: the render picks the last\nnode with startCycle <\e currentCycle, and nodes are kept sorted by it, so a\nfuture startCycle schedules the state.\n\nFills are 0..255 (255 \e full); pixel width \e fill * spriteWidth / 255.\ntransitionCycles \e tween duration; also the first term of the expiry deadline.\n\nNode payload (allocated via FUN_00129780, intrusive list):\n  +0x00 next  +0x08 prev\n  +0x10 def1RefCtr  +0x18 def1 (def+0x8 \e type id)\n  +0x20 def2RefCtr  +0x28 def2\n  +0x30 startCycle  +0x34 bar1FromFill  +0x38 bar2FromFill\n  +0x3c bar1ToFill  +0x40 bar2ToFill    +0x44 transitionCycles\nEngine Offsets.kt OHeadbar uses a base of node+0x10 (payload after the two list\npointers); its offsets are consistent, but CLIENTCYCLE_CREATED(+0x20 \e> +0x30)\nis really startCycle and DURATION_CLIENTCYCLES(+0x34 \e> +0x44) is really\ntransitionCycles.\n\nBars are bucketed per def id into 0x1b0-byte vector slots (ring+0x28..+0x38),\nsorted by def+0x38; each slot holds at most ring+0x8 nodes, capped at ring+0xc\nslots. Adding a duplicate startCycle overwrites that node in place.
