func=jag::PacketHandlers::CamRemoveroof	func_addr=0x001544c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt CAM_LOOKAT (opcode 0x58, fixed size 4). Sets/clears the camera look-at target. Reads [s32 packed coord via jag::Packet::g4_alt3]; if -1 clears (Camera+0x5e8\e0 disable, +0x5ec\e-1, +0x5f4\e0), else jag::game::BuildArea::DecodePackedCoord -> Camera+0x5e8\e1 (enable), +0x5ec\ecoord(x,y), +0x5f4\elevel; then bumps the camera-dirty marker at Client+0x19450 (+0x10 counter++, +0x14\e1). Camera \e Client+0x19420 (OClient.CAMERA \e jag::game::Camera). Unique signature (dedicated look-at-target fields + clear-on-(-1)); canonical token CAM_LOOKAT from the reference ServerProt label set. ENGINE DISCREPANCY: engine ServerProt.kt lists 0x58 as SET_BUILD_AREA_TARGET (MISC) -- WRONG; these are jag::game::Camera fields. Sibling op0x6f is the animated CAM_MOVETO (positional, left UNKNOWN pending eye/lookat disambiguation).
