func=jag::PacketHandlers::CamShake	func_addr=0x000ea6e0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eCAM_SHAKE direction\eSERVER opcode\e55 size\e6\n\nPayload: [0] g1_inv shakeMode, [1..2] g2_add param0, [3] g1 param1, [4] g1 param2, [5] g1 param3.\nDispatches a single virtual call on the OldCamera sub-object at Camera+0x248 (Camera \e\nclient+0x19420) through vftable+0x148, passing exactly FIVE arguments. The only camera API with a\n5-parameter signature is Shake(camera::ShakeMode,int,int,int,int); MoveTo/LookAt both take 7. The\nfield split (1 mode byte + 4 scalars) matches that arity exactly and sums to the 6-byte payload.\nNo coordinate promotion is done here, unlike CamMoveto / CamLookat.
func=jag::HitmarksAndHeadbars::RemoveHeadbar	func_addr=0x00492be0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::HitmarksAndHeadbars::RemoveHeadbar(HitmarksAndHeadbars* ring, int typeId)\n\nScans the 0x1b0-stride slot vector (ring+0x28..ring+0x30) for the slot whose\nfirst node's def (node+0x18) has id (def+0x8) \e\e typeId, then erases that ENTIRE\nslot via FUN_00490830 -- i.e. it drops every queued state for that headbar type,\nnot just the current one. Silently returns if no slot matches.\n\nIdentified by cross-version sig-scan from the verified 948-5 build\n(FUN_00626a40  -> tail call 0x00624df0); pattern\n"49 83 7A 40 00 74 ?? 4D 8B 1A 49 8B 43 18 3B 70 08" matched uniquely here.\nReached from the ext-info headbar sublist when the wire selector \e\e 0x7fff.
