func=jag::Packet::g4_alt1	func_addr=0x0011eb30	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::Packet::g4_alt1 — reads a uint32 from the packet buffer with byte order [+3]<<24 | [+2]<<16 | [+1]<<8 | [+0] (standard little-endian byte order, "alt1" form). Advances buffer position (+0x18) by 4. Reads 4 individual bytes from buffer (+0x10) at the current position and assembles them in LE order. The "alt1" naming distinguishes this from g4 (BE, gT_unsigned_int), g4_alt2 ([+2]<<24|[+3]<<16|[+0]<<8|[+1]), and g4_alt3. Ported 948-2-2 (0x00121ca0) -> 948-5 (0x00121e20): byte-exact 14-instruction match, no relocated immediates.
