func=jag::PacketHandlers::IfSetplayerhead	func_addr=0x00187bf0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eIF_SETPLAYERHEAD direction\eSERVER opcode\e24 size\e4\n\nPayload: g4_alt1 packed interface+component id. No further fields -- the value is taken from the\nclient itself.\nCalls jag::InterfaceManager::SetComponentProperty(mgr, componentId, kind\e3,\nvalue\eloggedInPlayer+0x48 (the local player id), extra\e0), which creates update entry type 4 and\nstores value/kind/extra in slots +0x20/+0x40/+0x60.\nEvidence for kind\e3 \e player head: the confirmed IF_SETNPCHEAD  uses kind\e2 with an npc\nid, and  uses kind\e1 with a bare model id -- i.e. the classic interface component\nmodel-type enum MODEL\e1, NPC_HEAD\e2, PLAYER_HEAD\e3. kind 3 and kind 5 each have exactly a\nself / snapshot / (u16+int) trio; kind 3 pairs with IF_SETPLAYERHEAD_SNAPSHOT  and\nkind 5 with the IF_SETPLAYERMODEL_* pair  / .\nResidual risk: the head-vs-model orientation rests on that enum ordering (kinds 1 and 2 are proven\nin-binary, 3 and 5 are inferred from it), not on a located consumer of the kind field.
