func=jag::LoginManager::SendLoginPacket	func_addr=0x001c5bf0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::LoginManager::SendLoginPacket — Builds and sends the login packet. First writes ~35 client preference/config fields (FUN_0017e910 over a local accumulator), then if all OK clears the ServerConnection message queue, builds the login body: opcode 0x3b4 path, ClientState/window-mode fields, CreateLoginRSAPacket (RSA block), username/password/auth strings, then tinyKeyEncrypt and dispatches via the login-variant SendClientMessage . On success initializes the ISAAC C2S and S2C ciphers (two 0x810-byte allocs; S2C key \e C2S key + 50 each int, delta const ). Ported from 948-2-2  via unique prologue sig-scan (LoginManager offsets +0xb98/+0xba0); confirmed by SendClientMessage call to 0x00c2b900. Was MISSING to auto-updater (relocated +0x1c0).
