func=jag::PacketHandlers::TelemetryGridAddColumn	func_addr=0x000fa300	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eTELEMETRY_GRID_ADD_COLUMN direction\eSERVER opcode\e220 size\e6\n\nPayload: [0] g1 gridIndex, [1] g1_sub insertIndex (-1 \e\e append), [2..5] g4 columnId.\nGrid table lives at client+DT_RELA[0xcf2], entries of 0x68 bytes indexed by gridIndex.\nCOLUMN (not ROW) proof: this handler grows the INNER vector at grid+0x8/0x10/0x18 (capacity 0x20\nbytes \e 8 entries) and then iterates every row-vector in grid+0x50, splicing one new cell\n(0x80000000 \e empty) at the insert index into each. Widening every existing row is by definition a\ncolumn insert. The sibling TelemetryGridAddRow appends a single new vector to grid+0x50 instead.
func=jag::PlayerList::GetLowResolutionPlayerPosition	func_addr=0x0015ab90	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::PlayerList::GetLowResolutionPlayerPosition(playerList, packet, playerIdx) — decodes one low-res player record in GPI (op22, PLAYER_INFO). Slot \e PlayerInfoSlot (+0 plane&3, +4 mapSquareX/regionX, +8 mapSquareY/regionY, +0x28 MoveSpeed*).\n[2] updateType:\n 0 \e ADD/PROMOTE to high-res: [1] recursePrev (if set, decode this slot's prior low-res move first), [6] localX, [6] localY, [1] queueExtInfo. World tile \e (mapSquareX*64 + localX, mapSquareY*64 + localY). Builds the high-res entity; then lazily reads appearance/spotanim sub-block via Packet::gScrambled* (count gScrambledUbyte, then per-anim shorts/uint). Returns 1 on promote.\n 1 \e FACE/rotate only: [2] rotation -> plane +\e rotation (&3).\n 2 \e SMALL local move: [5] \e dir8[2:0] (8-dir +/-1 on mapSquareX/Y) | planeDelta[4:3].\n 3 \e REGION jump: [20] \e regionY[7:0] | regionX[15:8] | plane[17:16] | moveSpeed[19:18]; each added to the slot fields (&0xff / &3); moveSpeed \e &MoveSpeed::enumArray[bits19:18].\nCORRECTED 2026-06-29: ADD-path 6-bit order is localX THEN localY (first read pairs with mapSquareX/regionX \e X axis; cross-confirmed vs beta GetLowResolutionPlayerPosition  where firstAxis uses regionX). VERIFIED 948-5.
