func=jag::game::CombinedLocationSection::MeshTrianglePickTest	func_addr=0x004d18c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=CombinedLocationSection mesh pick test (slot 0xa0 of vftable 0x01425520), the structural analogue of the Location pick test at 0x00481e70.\n\nEstablishes how a CombinedLocationSection reaches its renderable, and it is NOT through a render-node member of its own: the chain is section+0x08 (the GraphNode) -> +0x130 -> +0x1a0 (the attached entity) -> +0xf8 (the render model). Only after that third hop do the ORenderModel accesses appear - world transform at +0x30 and the mesh-component vector dereferenced off +0x268 - which is exactly the shape the Location pick test reaches directly off Location's own render-node slot.\n\nConsequence for the engine offset tables: a CombinedLocationSection render-node FIELD does not exist. The complete-object destructor (0x004b95f0) enumerates every refcounted member of the class and lists only +0xa8, +0x68, +0x58, +0x48 and +0x08, and sizeof is 0x110 - so the values the tables shipped for OCombinedLocationSection.RENDER_NODE / RENDER_NODE_CTRL / PARENT_COMBINED_LOCATION all fall past the end of the object and read whatever the pool allocator left there. They were copied from jag::game::Location, whose layout is unrelated to this class. Those three keys are withheld from the generated tables until someone models the GraphNode hop instead; withheld makes the engine throw, whereas the copied values silently returned garbage pointers.
