func=jag::PlayerEntityBaseAppearanceDecoder::DecodeBaseAppearanceAsPlayer	func_addr=0x00142770	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::PlayerEntityBaseAppearanceDecoder::DecodeBaseAppearanceAsPlayer. Decodes EQUIPMENT/BODY region of PLAYER_INFO APPEARANCE. this \e uint* (outer decoder obj +0x20). Markers copied from rodata WEARSLOT_MARKER_TEMPLATE : this[0]\eEMPTY(0), this[1]\eOBJ_MORPH(1, slot0-only), this[2]\eBODYPART_BASE(2), this[3]\eWORN_THRESHOLD(0x800). Per wear-slot: slot count \e cfg(off decoder+0x24 base, +0x260)+0x8; type[] @+0x10; slots with type\e\e1 emit NO byte. rev>\e0x3b5 (949) reads little-endian 7-bit LEB128 varint v; pre-949 read fixed g1(0\eempty) / g2 BE. v\e\ethis[0]->empty; slot0 && v\e\ethis[1]->obj-morph (gSmart2or4s+g1); v<this[3]->bodyPart id\ev-this[2]; else worn item id\ev-this[3]. Then recolorMask\eg2, per-type0-slot customisation blocks, ARRAY1\e10xg1, ARRAY2\e10xg1, BAS\eg2. vs 948: bodyPart BASE changed 0x100->2 (worn threshold 0x800 unchanged); empty/morph markers now data-driven (were hardcoded b0\e\e0 / v\e\e0xffff).
