func=jag::Client::DiscardPendingInput	func_addr=0x00272b80	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::Client::DiscardPendingInput -- drains the MOUSE recorder's two rings by copying each ring's\nwrite cursor into its read cursor, and blanks the sample records (button set to -1, coordinates\nzeroed, timestamps left alone). It also clears an unrelated hash table.\n\nIt does NOT touch the keyboard recorder's key ring or character ring. Any synthetic key entries\ntherefore survive a discard that would wipe synthetic mouse entries.
func=jag::game::ClientError::ReportFromException_Global	func_addr=0x0027c430	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=ClientError dispatcher (global reporter). Pulls the reporter sub-object from client+0x8b0 and the JagException message (param_2+8, SSO at +0x1f) + callstack (param_2+0xe58), then calls jag::game::ClientError::ReportError (FUN_006ef050) with flags\e7 (network report + callstack). Also processes a secondary object at client+0x930. Invoked by FatalSignalHandler when no per-thread SEH frame is set, and by the fatal handler FUN_00ad3ee0. Hooking ReportError (0x006ef050) neutralizes this path.
