func=jag::PacketHandlers::IfSetplayermodelSnapshot	func_addr=0x00187d50	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eIF_SETPLAYERMODEL_SNAPSHOT direction\eSERVER opcode\e147 size\e5\n\nPayload: 4-byte packed interface+component id; g1_inv snapshot slot.\nSetComponentProperty(mgr, componentId, kind\e5, value\e(-2 - slot), extra\e0) -- the snapshot form of\nIF_SETPLAYERMODEL_SELF , using the same -2-slot negative sentinel as the kind\e3\nsnapshot .\nResidual risk: see IF_SETPLAYERMODEL_SELF -- head-vs-model orientation follows the model-type enum\nordering, not a located consumer.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::CamForceangle	func_addr=0x000efbe0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eCAM_FORCEANGLE direction\eSERVER opcode\e79 size\e4\n\nPayload: g2 yaw (BE); g2_add pitch (BE, low byte -0x80).\nPasses both to FUN_0027c5e0 on the camera manager (Client+0x19420), which clamps pitch into\n[0x80,0x180], wraps yaw modulo 0x800, builds the orientation from (pitch*8, (0x400 - yaw)*8) via\nFUN_00ac7c10 and installs it on the active camera, interpolating over the camera's transition\nduration and setting the camera-dirty flag at +0x538.\nTwo angles driving the camera orientation directly \e CAM_FORCEANGLE.\nNOTE (out of scope, for whoever owns it): FUN_0027c5e0 is currently named\njag::packethandlers::ClientState::RUNCLIENTSCRIPT, which is wrong -- it is a camera-angle setter,\nnot a script dispatcher.
