func=jag::NPCList::ProcessNpcInfo	func_addr=0x001de9a0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=NPC_INFO handler (ServerProt op\e90, varShort). npcList \e *(this + 0xcfb-reloc). Capture-verified 949 wire (12/12 packets, official-successful-login-render.log). Layout:\ncount \e gBit(8)  # known NPCs to process\nPhase1 (count entries): hasUpdate\egBit(1); if 1: moveType\egBit(2): 0\eEXTONLY(queue,no bits) 1\eWALK[dir\egBit(3),hasExt\egBit(1)] 2\eRUN[big\egBit(1); big?dir1\egBit(3),dir2\egBit(3):dir\egBit(3); hasExt\egBit(1)] 3\eREMOVE(no bits)\nPhase2 add loop (while >\e16 bits remain): index\egBit(16)[0xFFFF terminates]; then per add record:\n  deltaX\egBit(coordW)  # signed, pairs playerTileX (@1224)\n  typeId\egBit(16)      # SetType vcall+0x220\n  hasExt\egBit(1)       # queue for ext-info\n  level\egBit(2)        # plane -> CoordFine.plane\n  facing\egBit(3)       # spawn dir angle\n  deltaY\egBit(coordW)  # signed, pairs playerTileY (@1225)\n  teleport\egBit(1)     # SetPosition vcall+0x170 arg\ncoordW \e *(npcList+0x428-reloc), set RAW by REBUILD_NORMAL(op64 ) body byte[6]; default 7.\nByte-align, then per hasExt NPC (phase1 first): [u16 BE blockLen][ext block] -> NPCEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo .\nNOTE 949 add-record field order DIFFERS from 948 (948 was index,flag,deltaY,deltaX,type,hasExt,level,facing).
