func=jag::game::PathingEntity::SetFinePosition	func_addr=0x004a5820	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=SetFinePosition(this, const float pos[3], bool immediate).\nWrites the entity's LIVE fine position, axis order {X, Z(height), Y}:\n  this+0x270 \e float xFine   this+0x274 \e float height   this+0x278 \e float yFine\nHeight is resampled from the terrain, not taken from pos[1].\nAlso seeds the render smoothing block: 0x280 startNs, 0x288/0x290/0x298 from(x,z,y) as double,\n0x2a0 endNs, 0x2a8/0x2b0/0x2b8 target(x,z,y) as double.\nReads this+0x2c0 (>0 \e> moving) to pick seq field +0xa60 vs +0xa64.
func=jag::opcode::oc_paramvalue	func_addr=0x00324220	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::opcode::oc_paramvalue — CS2 ObjType param value accessor (implicit-obj-context version). Pops 1 int from stack (param ID). Reads the active ObjType context from the script state at +0xbfe0 (if flag at +0x20 set) or +0xbfc0 (else). Looks up ParamType via ParamType::GetById equivalent. Then performs binary search through the obj's param list (puVar5[1] + 0x128, stride 0x28). Differentiates string vs int by comparing the ParamType's tag at +0x38 against the string-type marker: - String params: push value onto string stack (+0x10a8). - Int params: push via int stack (+0x100). Default value from ParamType +0x40 if no match found. Differs from item_getparam/mec_param which pop 2 ints (obj + param) — this uses the implicit active-obj context.
