func=jag::game::StatTable::UpdateStat	func_addr=0x000ed200	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::StatTable::UpdateStat -- ServerProt UPDATE_STAT decoder (949-1 opcode 4, fixed size 6).\n\nWire (6 bytes, exactly the declared fixed size):\n  g4_alt1 (readIntLittle)    experience\n  g1_add  (readUByteAdd)     currentLevel   -> byte + 0x80\n  g1_inv  (readUByteInverse) statId         -> -byte\n\nEntry \e statTable[+0x10] + statId*0x18 (StatEntry), matching engine OStatTable.TABLE_BEGIN\e0x10 /\nENTRY_SIZE\e0x18 and OStat INFO_PTR\e0x0 / XP_IN_TENTHS\e0x8 / EXPERIENCE\e0xc / REAL_LEVEL\e0x10 /\nCURRENT_LEVEL\e0x14.\nWrites experience, derives realLevel by scanning the StatType xp threshold array (count at\ninfo+0x18+8, uints at info+0x18+0x10) and clamping to info+0x4, writes currentLevel, then pushes\nstatId onto the 64-entry stat-refresh ring (Client-side base +0xc8, counter +0xd0, masked & 0x3f).\n\nStatEntry.xpInTenths is a SINGLE BYTE (CMP byte ptr [R9+0x8],0x0): when set the wire value is\nexperience*10 -- stored raw (capped 2,000,000,000) and divided by 10 for the level lookup; when\nclear it is capped at 200,000,000. Bytes +0x9..+0xb are padding the client never initialises, so a\n32-bit read of the flag picks up heap garbage and spuriously reports tenths mode. The F2P xp-cap\naccessor (FUN_003b3190) tests the same byte and divides the StatType cap by 10 when it is clear,\nconfirming the direction; the plain stat_xp accessor (FUN_003b30f0) returns experience unscaled,\nwhich is why normal accounts must run with the byte clear.\n\nEvidence: (1) exact three-way agreement between the decoded field order/offsets and the engine\nOStat/OStatTable tables; (2) prot table gives opcode 4 / size 6, and the 6 bytes read here are the\nwhole payload -- 948-5 UPDATE_STAT is likewise fixed 6; (3) engine STATTABLE_UPDATESTAT hook is live\nagainst this address. Note this is also a ServerProt handler; the sibling handlers in this DB use\nthe flat jag::PacketHandlers::* convention, but the class-qualified name is kept because it is the\nname the offset auto-updater relocates by.
