func=jag::game::InterfaceComponent::CreateByType	func_addr=0x00c39900	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Component factory for the CS2 CC_CREATE(parent, type, subId) opcode: given the cache/CS2 component type it allocates and returns the matching C++ subclass. Reached from jag::opcode::_cc_create and jag::opcode::CreateDynamicComponent, both of which also map the type through the 29-byte table at 0x01076260 to a ui-category byte for the parent's accept-child virtual - that byte is a category, not the type.\n\nDISPATCH: a 29-entry jump table at 0x010eaa54 (signed 32-bit offsets relative to the table base) covers types 0x00..0x1c. Five slots - 1, 2, 7, 8 and 25 - share the single invalid target 0x00c3bf30 and create nothing; none of those five appear anywhere in the CS2 corpus. The remaining 24 slots each have their own target, and the 24 are pairwise distinct classes:\n\n  - 13 types construct inline: the block allocates and stores its own vtable. Targets/vtables are\n    0(0x00c3b110/0x1436620) 3(0x00c3ae90/0x14365f0) 5(0x00c3aac0/0x14365c0) 9(0x00c3b490/0x14361d8)\n    10(0x00c3a430/0x1436008) 11(0x00c3a140/0x1435e38) 15(0x00c39b60/0x1435e08) 18(0x00c39f50/0x1435dd8)\n    19(0x00c39960/0x1435b30) 21(0x00c3ba70/0x14359e0) 26(0x00c3b710/0x14355d0) 27(0x00c3b900/0x14355a0)\n    28(0x00c3a810/0x1436450). All 13 differ.\n  - 11 types tail into a dedicated pooled factory, each with its OWN pool global and element stride:\n    4\e0x00224ba0 pool 0x1448da0 stride 0x1c8 vtable 0x1417668 | 6\e0x00264280 pool 0x1448d40 stride 0x3da0 vtable 0x1417698\n    12\e0x00224000 pool 0x1448ce0 stride 0x210 | 13\e0x00223300 pool 0x1448c80 stride 0x390\n    14\e0x00220460 pool 0x1448b60 stride 0x328 | 16\e0x00222540 pool 0x1448c20 stride 0x568\n    17\e0x0021e6b0 pool 0x1448a40 stride 0x5e8 | 20\e0x00221470 pool 0x1448bc0 stride 0x3d0\n    22\e0x0021f510 pool 0x1448b00 stride 0x250 | 23\e0x0022f120 pool 0x1448aa0 stride 0x2a8\n    24\e0x0021dc20 pool 0x14489e0 stride 0x1c8\n    Types 4 and 24 have the SAME element size but different pools and different factories, so size alone\n    does not identify a class here - the pool global does.\n\nCONSEQUENCE: type -> subclass is one-to-one over the 24 valid values, so a component's runtime type is fully recoverable from its vptr. It is NOT recoverable from any field: the type is consumed by this factory to pick the subclass and is never written back onto the object, which matches the CS2 corpus having no getter opcode for it. The value the tables previously carried as a component type field is the parent-layer component id (see jag::InterfaceManager::GetParentLayer and jag::opcode::_if_getlayer), so that key is withheld from the generated offset tables until a vptr-keyed mapping is built.\n\nSTILL TO DO before a vptr->type table can ship: the 13 inline vtables above were taken as the first vtable store on the block's path and have not been confirmed to be the PRIMARY vptr at object+0 (only types 4 and 6 were confirmed that way), and the whole table has to be re-derived for the PE build since vtable addresses are per-binary.
func=jag::HintArrow::~HintArrow	func_addr=0x00284b50	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::HintArrow::~HintArrow (complete-object dtor D1, vtable slot 0). Walks the vtable chain HintArrow -> Entity base -> GraphNode base: DecRefs target-entity shared_ptr at +0x88, DecRefs Entity shared_ptr at +0x48, then Detach + delete GraphNode at +0x8. Does NOT free (complete-object variant). Paired deleting dtor (D0) is the _deleting variant.
