func=jag::game::WorldAreaType::DecodeType	func_addr=0x00557350	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::WorldAreaType::DecodeType(this, jag::Packet&, opcode). Config group/archive 83 (see ConfigProvider::RegisterConfigGroupIds _DAT_01692a44\e0x53; loaded via list slot ConfigProvider+0x1e0). Opcodes:\n op2: g3 (3-byte BE) -> this+0x38. The friend's "colour" field (RGB24 key for the worldmap fromColour lookup). Stored verbatim, not masked.\n op3: two g4 packed coords via BuildArea::DecodePackedCoord -> rbtree @this+0x70 (node 0x38B: +0x20 sw-coord key, +0x2c ne-coord\einit 0xffffffff, +0x28 int val). A rectangle list.\n op4: one g4 packed coord + one g4 int -> rbtree @this+0x40 (node 0x30B: +0x20 coord key, +0x28 int val, +0x2c int). A per-coord value list.\n Both op3/op4 also expand a bbox @this+0xa0 via (coord.x>>6, coord.y>>6) \e map-square granularity.\n Packed coord (DecodePackedCoord ~0x7b0650): plane\e(v>>28)&3, x\e(v>>14)&0x3fff, y\ev&0x3fff, 0xffffffff\enull. g4 reader \e jag::Packet::gT&lt;unsigned_int&gt;  (BE u32).
func=jag::ClientProt::PopEventMouseMoveSample	func_addr=0x001754e0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::PopEventMouseMoveSample -- vtable slot 4. Pops the oldest movement sample and\nadvances MouseInputRecorder::moveRingRead, or returns NULL when the ring is empty. Reaches the\nrecorder through sender->client -> MainLogicManager -> its MouseInputRecorder sub-object.\n\nThe read cursor is advanced for EVERY pop, including samples the caller then discards under the\nsame-position elision rule, so an elided sample is still consumed.\n\nProof of the two-ring layout: MainLogicManager's MouseInputRecorder holds a 50-slot press ring\nfollowed by its cursor pair, then a 200-slot movement ring followed by ITS cursor pair. Confirmed\nthree ways: this pop, the two init loops in jag::MainLogicManager::Construct (each followed by an\n8-byte store clearing exactly that ring's cursor pair), and jag::Client::DiscardPendingInput,\nwhich drains both rings by copying write into read.
