func=jag::game::SetInteractionMarkerEntry	func_addr=0x0022ac10	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=SetInteractionMarkerEntry: creates/updates a kind-0xe (14) update entry on manager param_1 via\njag::InterfaceManager::CreateOrFindUpdateEntry. param_2\e\e0 \e> remove entry (FUN_00229ed0 \e clear).\nEntry layout written:\n  +0x20 block1: {u32 0xffffffff, float coordA_X_fine\eparam_3, u32 0, float coordA_Y_fine\eparam_4}\n  +0x40 target: {i32 type\eparam_5, i32 entityId\eparam_6}  (tag +0x58; prev target released via\n                PTR_FUN_01430b80[tag] then tag set to 1)\n  +0x60 block2: {u32 mode\eparam_9, float coordB_X_fine\eparam_7, u32 0, float coordB_Y_fine\eparam_8}\nCallers: SetInteractionTarget (op2, server-auth) sets it; the client-side click predictors\nFUN_00160c40/FUN_00161250 and the per-frame marker renderer FUN_002a4880 clear it (param_2\e0)\nwhen the local player reaches the target.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::NpcAnimSpecific	func_addr=0x000f2320	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eNPC_ANIM_SPECIFIC direction\eSERVER opcode\e35 size\e19\n\nPayload (19 bytes): g2 npcIndex @0; g1_sub delay @2 (-0x80 - b); 4x 4-byte little-endian\nint @3,7,11,15 forming a contiguous 4-int animation block passed by address.\n\nEvidence (three converging lines):\n 1. Deterministic size bucket: the only size-19 unnamed SERVER handler in 949-4 and\n    NPC_ANIM_SPECIFIC is the only size-19 unassigned official name.\n 2. Structurally IDENTICAL to jag::PacketHandlers::PlayerAnimSpecific \n    (PLAYER_ANIM_SPECIFIC, opcode 203, size 17): same 4-int block, same trailing\n    transformed byte, same virtual dispatch through vftable+0x1e0. The 2-byte delta\n    (19 vs 17) is exactly this packet's leading npcIndex, which the player form omits\n    because it resolves the active player instead.\n 3. Entity resolution is jag::NPCList::GetNPCNode (vs game::GetActivePlayer in the\n    player form), and the 4th argument to the vftable+0x1e0 call is 1 here vs 0 there\n    - the player/npc entity-kind discriminator.
