func=jag::PacketHandlers::PointlightEnabled	func_addr=0x001e3e60	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\ePOINTLIGHT_ENABLED direction\eSERVER opcode\e162 size\e3\n\nPayload: g2 pointlight id (BE); g1 flags -- low nibble \e value (0xf means "clear override"),\nbit 0x10 suppresses the shadow/fade recompute.\nResolves every scene pointlight instance carrying that id (FUN_004ad4d0 on the light manager\nClient+0x19558) and sets light+0x150 \e (value \e\e 1) with the override flag at light+0x151, then\nresets the fade weight light+0xe8 and recomputes the shadow blend light+0x114.\nEvidence: the per-frame light update FUN_006be940 gates the light entirely on this pair --\n"if (light+0x151 \e\e 0 || light+0x150 !\e 0) fade IN else fade OUT and release the shadow map", and\nlater re-reads it as the override of the light type's own enable flag at type+0x1c. That is the\nenable/disable field.\nSibling override pairs on the same object: +0x152/+0x153 shadow, +0x154/+0x155 extend-above,\n+0x156/+0x157 extend-below.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::PointlightShadow	func_addr=0x001e30a0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\ePOINTLIGHT_SHADOW direction\eSERVER opcode\e212 size\e3\n\nPayload: pointlight id + value byte (0xf clears the override), same shape as the other\nPOINTLIGHT_* boolean packets.\nSets light+0x152 with the override flag at light+0x153 on every scene light matching the id.\nEvidence: both the per-frame light update FUN_006be940 and POINTLIGHT_ENABLED  read\nthis pair as "castsShadow \e light+0x153 ? light+0x152 : lightType+0xae", and use the result to\ndrive the shadow blend light+0x114 (set to light+0x118 when true, 0 when false), gated on\nlightType+0x80 (shadow strength) being non-zero. That is unambiguously the shadow flag.
