func=jag::ClientProt::SendMessagePublic	func_addr=0x00313350	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=NAME RETRACTED: this is NOT MESSAGE_PUBLIC. op101 varByte (descriptor 0x01683ef0, registered at 0x000e5782). Pops 2 CS2 strings + 2 CS2 ints. Wire: [p1 total \e nameLen+msgLen+3][pStr name][p1 int0-1][p1 (int1\e\e1)][message, UTF8->CP1252, clamped to 0x50 chars, pStringNoConversion]. It carries a TARGET NAME, has no Huffman body and no mute/chat guard. The real public-chat emitter is 0x00313e00 (op35 varByte): one string, colour table 0x01444160 (12) + effect table 0x01444040 (6), mute guard, [p1 size][p1 colour][p1 effect][Huffman via 0x007b3750] - chat payload + effects with NO target name.
