func=jag::game::VarBitType::DecodeType	func_addr=0x004fc940	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::VarBitType::DecodeType. Opcode 1: reads varDomainType byte then smart2or4 varId, resolves varType via ConfigProvider::GetVarType, stores shared_ptr at this+0x38/+0x40. Opcode 2: reads two bytes into startBit (this+0x48) and endBit (this+0x4c). Opcode 0x10: sets flag byte at this+0x50. NOTE: schema drift vs older references which only had opcodes 1 and 2 (opcode 0x10 is newer). PostDecode is an empty stub. GetVarBitMask/SetVarBitValue/GetVarBitValue are likely inlined in this release build (not separately identifiable).
func=jag::PacketHandlers::IfSetmodel	func_addr=0x00187cd0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eIF_SETMODEL direction\eSERVER opcode\e101 size\e8\n\nPayload: [0..3] g4 componentId, [4..7] g4 modelId (BE).\nCalls jag::InterfaceManager::SetComponentProperty (update-entry kind 4, the component model-source\noverride with three slots at entry+0x20/+0x40/+0x60) with sourceType\e1, primary\emodelId,\nsecondary\e-1. This is byte-for-byte the same call shape as the already-named IfSetnpchead\n(0x00187280), which uses sourceType\e2 with an npc id and the same -1 secondary. sourceType 3 and 5\nare the player-model / player-head families (each with self, snapshot and other variants).\nsourceType 1 with a single plain id and no entity indirection is the plain model source.
