func=jag::HitmarksAndHeadbars::DrawHeadbar	func_addr=0x002081f0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::HitmarksAndHeadbars::DrawHeadbar(ctx, owner, def, fromFill, toFill,\n                                      transitionCycles, elapsed, outW, outH)\n\ndef \e group-72 headbar def. Sprite pair chosen by owner vtable+0x190 size class:\n0 -> (def+0x50 back, def+0x54 front); 1 -> (def+0x58, def+0x5c);\n2 -> (def+0x60, def+0x64). def+0x6c/+0x70 are end-cap sprites; def+0x68 !\e 0\nselects the alternate blitter. def+0x30 \e the type loader.\n\nFill -> pixels: width \e fill * spriteWidth / 255 (255 \e full bar). A non-zero\nfromFill clamps the drawn width to >\e 2px.\n\nTWEEN (elapsed < transitionCycles):\n    step \e def[0x48]\n    w \e fromPx + ((elapsed/step)*step * (toPx - fromPx)) / transitionCycles\n  step quantises the animation; step \e\e 0 disables the tween (w stays at\n  fromPx). Alpha is fully opaque here.\n\nHOLD + FADE (elapsed >\e transitionCycles): bar is drawn at toPx, and\n    if def[0x44] < 0            -> no fade, fully opaque\n    else t \e elapsed - transitionCycles\n         alpha256 \e (def[0x4c] - t) * 256 / (def[0x4c] - def[0x44])\n         t <\e def[0x44]  -> opaque\n         t >\e def[0x4c]  -> transparent\n  So def+0x44 \e cycles after the tween before fading starts, def+0x4c \e cycles\n  after the tween at which the bar is gone. def+0x4c is the same term\n  UpdateAndRenderHeadbars uses to expire the node, so fade-out and removal\n  coincide exactly.
