func=jag::game::HeadbarType::DecodeType	func_addr=0x0056db40	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=WARNING - NAME IS SUSPECT. This is registered for CONFIG GROUP 46\n(ConfigProvider::EnsureTypeListsLoaded slot +0x158, DAT_01692888), but\njag::HitmarksAndHeadbars::AddHeadbar  looks up its headbar defs from\nCONFIG GROUP 72 (DAT_016929c0 \e 0x48, slot +0x150). The bar geometry/timing\nfields the headbar render actually reads are incompatible with this class:\n\n  this+0x40 here \e 24-bit colour (op2, ctor default 0xffffff), but the headbar\n                   render reads def+0x40 as a pixel height\n  this+0x68 here \e eastl::string (op8; SSO marker at this+0x7f \e 0x17), but the\n                   headbar draw reads def+0x68 as a byte flag and def+0x6c /\n                   def+0x70 as sprite ids -- which would fall inside the string\n\nSo the def consumed by AddHeadbar/DrawHeadbar is NOT this type. Do not rename\neither function on the assumption they share a class until group 46 vs 72 is\nresolved. (Object layout here is solid: 0xd8 alloc, ref_counter_base at +0x0,\nclass base at +0x20, id at base+0x8, DecodeType this \e class base.)\n\nHYPOTHESIS: "HeadbarType" belongs on the group-72 type instead, and this class\nis something else. Server-side world.gregs.voidps HeadbarDecoder mirrors THIS\nopcode table under Config.HIT_BARS \e 46, and Config.SKY_BOXES \e 72 -- one of\nthose two names is wrong. Needs confirmation before any rename.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::MapAnim	func_addr=0x000f0a40	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=MAP_ANIM (S2C, top-op 173, zone sub-op idx 15, size 11). Spawns tile spot-anim via FUN_00aeed60. 949 wire (all raw/BE, no +-0x80 transforms):\n+0 g1  packedCoord \e (localX&7)<<4 | (localY&7)   [X\ehi nibble +baseTileX, Y\elo nibble +baseTileY]\n+1 g4(BE) spotanimId (graphic id; FUN_007abdc0 lookup)\n+5 g1  byte5: lo3\erotation(&7), hi-nibble\e(b&0xf0)<<5 -> direction/angle\n+6 g1  loopCount/duration (0 \e play once)\n+7 g1  heightOffset (scaled to float)\n+8 g2(BE) scale/size (default 256 if 0)\n+10 g1 selector (0/1 -> priority arg 6 or 8) -- MAP_ANIM-only; SOUND_AREA(op160) omits this byte
