func=jag::ClientProt::SendMessagePrivate	func_addr=0x00315d20	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::SendMessagePrivate — XTEA-encrypted PM VARIANT. Descriptor 0x01684020, registered id 82 size -2 \e> ClientProt op82 (var_short). Consumes 3 CS2 strings + 2 CS2 ints. Wire: [op82][size:u16][pStr A][pStr B][p1 C][p1 (D\e\e1) bool][pStr E (message)][+7 pad][Packet::tinyKeyEncrypt over the body]. IMPORTANT: this is NOT the free-text PM the retail client emits — live capture shows the user's free-text PM (lobby AND in-world) is op71 (jag::opcode::ChatSendPrivate / CHAT_SENDPRIVATE, Huffman body, no XTEA). op82 is a distinct encrypted 3-string message variant, not observed in captured PM flows. The server's op82\eMESSAGE_PRIVATE label is misplaced: MESSAGE_PRIVATE belongs on op71.
