func=jag::PacketHandlers::CamLookat	func_addr=0x000efa30	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eCAM_LOOKAT direction\eSERVER opcode\e42 size\e6\n\nPayload: [0] g1_sub accel, [1] g1 localX, [2..3] g2 height (<<2), [4] g1 localZ, [5] g1_inv speed.\nLocal tile coords are promoted to world coords as (local + camBase)*512 + 256 using the Camera\nobject at client+0x19420 (CAMERA in the engine offset table), fields +0x60c / +0x608.\n\nLOOKAT (not MOVETO) proof: the helper it calls (0x0027c290) drives the camera controller group at\nctrl+0x30/0x38/0x40 via setter 0x00aedf70. That group's mode factory (0x00668540) builds 5 distinct\nclasses across 7 modes (4 non-spline + 1 shared spline class), matching the 5 Lookat* mode classes;\nthe sibling group at ctrl+0x48/0x50/0x58 builds only 3 classes, matching the 3 Position* classes.\nIndependently, this group's element getter is invoked with one out-parameter\n(GetLookatData(LookatData&)) whereas the sibling group's getter takes an out-parameter plus a double\n(GetPositionData(PositionData&,double)). MOVETO is the sibling handler CamMoveto.
