func=jag::game::Entity::~Entity	func_addr=0x004d8dc0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=1696	cu_index_from_entry=364	text=PathingEntity::NAME is an eastl::fixed_string<char,64> BASED AT this+0x90, spanning 0x90..0xf7:\n  0x90 mpBegin | 0x98 mnSize | 0xa0 mnCapacity|heapMask (0x800000000000003F)\n  0xa7 SSO/heap marker | 0xa8 allocator slot (NEVER written by the ctor)\n  0xb0 mpPoolBegin -> 0xb8 | 0xb8..0xf7 inline 64-byte buffer\nNext members confirm the span: eastl::string at 0xf8 (marker 0x10f) and at 0x110 (marker 0x127).\n\e> engine offsets LAST_MOVESPEED\e0x98, NEXT_X_OFFSET_FINE\e0xa0, NEXT_Y_OFFSET_FINE\e0xa8 are ALL\ninside this string header and are invalid.
func=jag::MainLogicManager::KeyboardInputRecorder::OnKeyChar	func_addr=0x00766260	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::MainLogicManager::KeyboardInputRecorder::OnKeyChar -- producer of the SECOND keyboard ring,\nthe typed-character ring. Pushes a KeyEvent of the identical record type as the key ring but with\nkeyId \e -1, rawKeyCode \e -1, charCode \e the typed character, repeat \e 0 and modifierMask reduced\nto its low three bits. Same 255-slot, drop-oldest wrap rule as the key ring, with its own cursor\npair immediately after the array.\n\nThe two rings are laid out back to back with homogeneous records, which is what makes it possible\nfor a downstream stage to merge them into a single per-tick list.\n\nOPEN QUESTION (do not assume): whether typed characters reach the server at all. The\nserver-bound key stage writes only the LOW BYTE of keyId per record and filters on repeat being\nclear; a char record would satisfy that filter and would serialise as 0xFF. Either the stage's\nsource list excludes char records, or char records are what the 0xFF-keyed entries are. Not\nresolved in this pass -- confirm by capture before building a producer for it.\n\nName provenance: descriptive project coinage. The engine's existing OnKeyCharInner capture hook\nsits upstream of this delegate.
