func=jag::PacketHandlers::TelemetryGridAddRow	func_addr=0x001179b0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eTELEMETRY_GRID_ADD_ROW direction\eSERVER opcode\e184 size\e6\n\nPayload: [0] g1_inv insertIndex (-1 \e\e append), [1] g1 gridIndex, [2..5] g4 rowId.\nGrid table lives at client+DT_RELA[0xcf2], entries of 0x68 bytes indexed by gridIndex.\nROW (not COLUMN) proof: this handler operates on the OUTER vector at grid+0x20/0x28/0x30 (capacity\n0xA0 bytes \e 40 entries) and appends ONE new cell-vector to grid+0x50, sized from the length of the\ninner vector at grid+0x8. Adding a row therefore creates exactly one new vector whose width is the\ncurrent column count. The sibling TelemetryGridAddColumn instead grows the inner list at grid+0x8\n(capacity 0x20 \e 8 entries) and inserts one cell into EVERY existing row-vector.
func=jag::game::World::World	func_addr=0x004c4d80	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::World::World(this, sceneManager, RT7Core, Js5ResourceProvider, ConfigProvider, PlayerVarDomain, AssetBuilder, worldArea<WorldAreaType>&, BuildMode(\e3), swMapSquareX(p10), swMapSquareY(p11), neMapSquareX(p12), neMapSquareY(p13), levelHeightGrid&).\nStores the two map-square CORNERS: this+0x13fb4\eswMapSquareX, +0x13fb8\eswMapSquareY, +0x13fbc\eneMapSquareX, +0x13fc0\eneMapSquareY (plane/level count\e3 at +0xa4118).\nThen width \e neX-swX (this+0x13ff0), height \e neY-swY (this+0x13ff4), maxDim (this+0x13ff8), and allocates the World's 2D map-square cell grid (this+0x2800 vector-of-vectors of jag::game::MapSquareStatus) sized (width+1) columns x (height+1) rows.\n\e> the two REBUILD_NORMAL packed coords ARE this World's map-square grid SW & NE corners \e the world area's bounding rectangle / coordinate window (grid origin \e SW corner). Cross-confirmed in librs2client.so jag::game::World::World: stores param_9..param_12 at +0x10e88/+0x10e8c/+0x10e90/+0x10e94 then iVar19\efield_0x10e90-field_0x10e88 (width), iVar29\efield_0x10e94-field_0x10e8c (height) — same logic, offsets drifted.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::MapProjanim	func_addr=0x000f1f80	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=MAP_PROJANIM (S2C, top-op 132, zone sub-op idx 4, size 20). Tile->tile projectile via jag::ProjectileList::Add. Target is a TILE (source + signed dx/dy), NOT an entity index; lockon uses static defaults &DAT_01446f18. 949 wire (raw/BE); DISASM-verified consumes bytes 0..16, then advances pos to +20 (bytes 17,18,19 RESERVED/unread -> server writes 3 pad bytes):\n+0  g1  srcCoord \e (localX&7)<<3 | (localY&7) | flag<<7   [X bits3-5 +baseTileX, Y bits0-2 +baseTileY, bit7\eflag arg7]\n+1  g1s targetDeltaY (signed, tiles from src)\n+2  g1s targetDeltaX (signed)\n+3  g3(BE) medium (ProjectileList::Add arg6; role uncertain -- confirm)\n+6  g2(BE) spotanimId/graphicId (0xffff \e no projectile, gate)\n+8  g1s startHeight (<<4 fine)\n+9  g1s endHeight (<<4 fine)\n+10 g2(BE) startTime/delay [inferred]\n+12 g2(BE) endTime/lifetime [inferred]\n+14 g1  alpha (0xff \e default opaque; ProjectileList::Add param_17)\n+15 g2(BE) angle/lockonSlot (<<2) [inferred]\n+17..19 RESERVED (3 bytes, unread)
