func=jag::NPCEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo	func_addr=0x0016c0c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=339	cu_index_from_entry=72	text=COMBAT_LEVEL_HEADBAR_ID (NPC ext-info bit22, 0x400000). Reads 1 gScrambledShort, selector  \e mode 0 \e g2 (plain BE). Stores raw u16 at entity+0x1158. Sentinel 0xFFFF -> RESTORE DEFAULT from the NpcType (copies NpcType+0x2a8 into entity+0x1158; branch jumps 0x00170198). Plain id override, NO ref-counted entity cache. This is the REAL combat-level/headbar-id override. Server encode: writeShort(id) / writeShort(0xFFFF) to restore. NOTE: prior Rev949NpcUpdateMaskKey put COMBAT_LEVEL_HEADBAR_ID on bit10 -- that was a MISLABEL of FACE_ENTITY (bit10, LE short + ref-counted cache). Correct: FACE_ENTITY\ebit10, COMBAT_LEVEL_HEADBAR_ID\ebit22. CONFIRMED 949-1.
func=jag::NPCEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo	func_addr=0x0016c0c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=418	cu_index_from_entry=84	text=ANIMATION / seq (NPC ext-info bit3). Reads 4x gSmart2or4s (BE big-smart anim-layer ids; 0x7fff\e-1\eempty layer) then 1 gScrambledByte delay/speed, selector  \e mode 1 \e g1_add (wire \e val+0x80 \e readByteAdd). Dispatches vtable+0x1e0 (RequestAnimation; concrete FUN_004e4190) -> per-layer SeqType lookup + duration (+0xa48) -> stores 4 ids at entity+0x2c8, delay at +0xb60, duration at +0xb64. Server encode: 4x writeBigSmart(layerId, empty\e0x7fff) + writeByteAdd(delay). CONFIRMED 949-1.
func=jag::NPCEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo	func_addr=0x0016c0c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=546	cu_index_from_entry=112	text=NPC HITS NARROW block (mask bit0 / 0x1). Mode table @NpcHitsNarrowModeTable(0xd66cdd)\e{03 02 00 01 01 02 00}. Legacy small-damage channel (damage \e smart).\nWIRE:\n  hitmarkCount : gScrambledByte mode3\eSUBTRACT\n  per hitmark: type\egSmart1or2 ; damage\egSmart1or2 [0x7ffe: soak byte gScrambledByte mode2\eINVERSE ; 0x7fff: type2,damage,soak,extra all gSmart1or2] ; delay\egSmart1or2\n  headbarCount : gScrambledByte mode0\ePLAIN\n  per headbar: type/sel/duration\egSmart1or2 ; front\egScrambledByte mode1\eADD ; [twoFill]back(bar1)\eADD ; transId\egSmart1or2Minus1 ; [transId>\e0] front2\egScrambledByte mode2\eINVERSE, [twoFill]back2\egScrambledByte mode0\ePLAIN
func=jag::NPCEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo	func_addr=0x0016c0c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=2567	cu_index_from_entry=525	text=FACE_TILE (NPC ext-info bit6). Reads 2 gScrambledShort: s1 selector \emode0\eg2 (BE), s2 selector \emode2\eg2_add (BE low+0x80). Stored as floats: faceX\e(s1-1)>>1 at entity+0x22c, faceY\e(s2-1)>>1 at entity+0x234, and entity+0x230\e0. Values are in HALF-TILE units (wire \e tile*2 + 1 \e tile centre). Persistent static face-point (not re-resolved to a moving entity). Server encode: writeShort(x*2+1) + writeShortAdd(y*2+1). CONFIRMED 949-1.
func=jag::NPCEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo	func_addr=0x0016c0c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=2705	cu_index_from_entry=546	text=NPC HITS WIDE block (mask bit32). Mode table @NpcHitsWideModeTable(0xd66c88)\e{00 03 02 03 00 00 02}. THE live-combat channel for NPCs (32-bit damage).\nWIRE (read order):\n  hitmarkCount : gScrambledByte mode0\ePLAIN          (server writeByte)\n  per hitmark:\n    type       : gSmart1or2                          (writeSmart)\n    damage     : g4Scrambled mode3\einverse-middle    (writeIntInverseMiddle)  [0x7ffe form: soak via gScrambledByte mode3\eSUBTRACT]\n    [0x7fff big form: type2(smart), damage\eg4Scrambled mode3, soak\esmart, extra\eg4Scrambled mode2\eMIDDLE]\n    delay      : gSmart1or2\n  headbarCount : gScrambledByte mode2\eINVERSE         (writeByteInverse)\n  per headbar:\n    type/sel/duration : gSmart1or2 (sel 0x7fff\eremove)\n    front      : gScrambledByte mode3\eSUBTRACT\n    [twoFill] back(bar1): gScrambledByte mode0\ePLAIN\n    transId    : gSmart1or2Minus1\n    [transId>\e0] front2: gScrambledByte mode0\ePLAIN ; [twoFill] back2: gScrambledByte mode2\eINVERSE
func=jag::NPCEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo	func_addr=0x0016c0c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=2884	cu_index_from_entry=571	text=FACE_ENTITY (NPC ext-info bit10). Reads 1 gScrambledShort, selector  \e mode 1 \e g2LE (little-endian u16 \e readUShortLittle). Stores raw 16-bit target index at entity+0x10d0 (0xffff -> stores -1). On every update it clears the ref-counted RESOLVED-entity cache at entity+0xf40/+0xf48 (DecRef old ptr) so the render loop re-resolves the index to a live entity and re-orients toward it EACH FRAME \e TRACKED (distinct from one-shot FACE_DIRECTION/FACE_TILE). Sentinel 0xFFFF \e stop facing (clear cache + index\e-1). Server encode: writeShortLittle(index) / writeShortLittle(0xFFFF) to clear. Player-vs-NPC discrimination inside the index value \e classic RS convention (HYPOTHESIS, capture-verify). CONFIRMED (read/store/sentinel/tracked) 949-1.
func=jag::NPCEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo	func_addr=0x0016c0c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=11072	cu_index_from_entry=2106	text=FACE_ENTITY (npc bit10) handler: gScrambledShort mode1 \e g2LE (writeShortLittle), zero-extended full 16-bit (0..0xFFFF). 0xFFFF -> stop (stores -1 at renderNode+0x10d0, DecRef+clear resolved cache +0xf40/+0xf48). Else stores RAW 16-bit index (NO transform/mask) and clears resolved cache to force per-frame re-resolve against the combined entity table. Player-vs-NPC discrimination is entirely in the deferred resolve (NOT confirmed here): likely players\e0x8000|playerIndex, npcs\eraw index, but capture-verify before locking encoder.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::TelemetryGridMoveRow	func_addr=0x00117710	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eTELEMETRY_GRID_MOVE_ROW direction\eSERVER opcode\e223 size\e3\n\nPayload: g1_inv from index; g1_sub grid index; g1_inv to index.\nCalls FUN_006c1840(grid, from, to), which moves one element in THREE parallel per-row vectors --\ngrid+0x20 (int), grid+0x38 (the pin vector) and grid+0x50 (the 0x18-byte row records that hold\neach row's cell array) -- then re-normalises the pin vector so every non -1 entry equals its own\nindex. Moving the whole row record \e> MOVE_ROW.\nContrast TELEMETRY_GRID_MOVE_COLUMN , which instead moves one element inside the\ncolumn-header vector at grid+0x8 AND inside every row's cell array.
func=jag::ClientProt::SendFriendlistAdd	func_addr=0x003c8010	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=CONFIRMED FRIENDLIST_ADD for 949-4. Descriptor 0x016842e0 registered at opcode 38, size -1/varByte (RegisterAll). Add-only guards mirroring IGNORELIST_ADD at 0x0031f710: list-full ("Your friends list is full (200/400 ...)"), self-add rejection, IsOnFriendsList -> "is already on your friends list", IsOnIgnoreList -> "Please remove <name> from your ignore list first". Payload is a single jag-string (the display name).
