func=jag::game::PathingEntity::SetSize	func_addr=0x004a6600	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=SetSize(this, newSize). Entity tile size lives at this+0x184. Because the fine position is the\nentity's CENTRE, a size delta shifts it by delta*512*0.5 on BOTH horizontal axes — which is what\nproves this+0x270 and this+0x278 are the horizontal (X, Y) floats and this+0x274 is height.\nMOVSS at 0x004a5f0e/0x004a5f29 read them as float; MOVSS at 0x004a5f2f/0x004a5f35 write them back.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::ObjAdd	func_addr=0x00116e30	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OBJ_ADD — ServerProt op46, FIXED size 5 (confirmed: ZoneUpdates::BindHandlers slot 0x015c1c40->op46 + authoritative 948-5 prot table). Reads 5 bytes from PacketCore (position@+0x18, bufData@+0x10):\n  body[0] packedCoord  g1 raw: xInZone\e(b>>4)&7, yInZone\eb&7 -> abs tile (g_baseTileX+x, g_baseTileY+y)\n  body[1..2] COUNT     g2 (BE, clean)  -> AddObjStack count -> ItemStack+0x4 ITEM_AMOUNT\n  body[3..4] OBJID     g2_add (hi raw, lo readUByteAdd\e(lo-0x80)&0xff) -> AddObjStack objId -> ItemStack+0x0 ITEM_ID\nNo count\e\e255 escape; fixed 5 bytes. Sample 54 00 01 03 32 \e tile(5,4 in zone), count\e1, objId\e(0x03<<8)|((0x32-0x80)&0xff)\e0x3B2\e946\e'knife'.\nPRIOR comment had objId/count SWAPPED (it claimed body[1..2]\eobjId) — corrected via 3 independent sources: engine OItemStack(ID@0,AMT@4) + live capture (body[1..2] always 0x0001 across 5 distinct spawns) + gamevals (946 knife / 558 mindrune / 1511 logs / 1923 bowl_empty / 1931 pot_empty). Server encoder order: p1 packedCoord; p2 count; p2_add objId — the byte-reverse of the older id-first layout.
