func=jag::PlayerList::HandleAbsolutePlayerPositions	func_addr=0x00b067e0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=WALK-ANIM ROOT CAUSE: local player slot+0x28 (MoveSpeed) is hardcoded to &enumArray[0]\eSTATIONARY here (puVar9[5]\e&DAT_015bf210). Low-res players get enumArray[(v>>18)&3]. Since single-tile GPI walks (moveType 1 flag\e0) never change slot+0x28, a GPI-driven local player stays at STATIONARY MoveSpeed -> SelectBaseAnimation plays the STAND anim while the position lerps \e glide with no legs. Live likely client-predicts the local player instead of GPI-driving it.
func=jag::PlayerList::HandleAbsolutePlayerPositions	func_addr=0x00b067e0	kind=plate	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Setting prototype: void HandleAbsolutePlayerPositions(void *this, PacketCore *packet)
func=jag::PlayerList::HandleAbsolutePlayerPositions	func_addr=0x00b067e0	kind=eol	insn_offset_from_entry=69	cu_index_from_entry=19	text=GPI INIT step 1: gBit(30) \e local player absolute packed coord. DecodePackedCoord: plane\e(v>>28)&3, x\e(v>>14)&0x3fff, y\ev&0x3fff. (Burthorpe login \e plane0,x2897,y3538.)
func=jag::PlayerList::HandleAbsolutePlayerPositions	func_addr=0x00b067e0	kind=eol	insn_offset_from_entry=846	cu_index_from_entry=186	text=GPI INIT step 2 (per low-res slot, idx 1..0x7FF skipping local \e> 2046 reads): gBit(20) \e [moveSpeed:2 (v>>18&3)][plane:2 (v>>16&3)][xHi:8 (v>>8&0xff)][yHi:8 (v&0xff)]. Coarse coord stored via DecodePackedCoord((plane<<28)|(xHi<<14)|yHi). NOTE beta reads gBit(18) (no moveSpeed); target\e20.
