func=jag::HintArrowPointer::MainLogic	func_addr=0x0013dee0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::HintArrowPointer::MainLogic (Entity vtable slot +0x70). Per-frame update of the 3D pointer model: if model (this+0x70) loaded, take GraphNode world matrix, apply HeightMap level transform, write the model matrix, and enqueue {ctrl@+0x68, model@+0x70} into the global render-collection list. HintArrow inherits the empty base at this slot (HintArrow::MainLogic is a no-op). Installed in HintArrowPointer vtable slot 14.
func=jag::Js5MasterIndex::Js5MasterIndex	func_addr=0x00b5ca60	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Js5MasterIndex ctor. Parses blob (packet param_4): pos\e1; gT_u32 (signature-region length); byte@5 \e archiveCount (bVar4); param_1[0]\ecount-1. Entries table \e count*0x50 bytes from offset 6. Trailing RSA signature.\nVERIFICATION (2 gates, BOTH must pass or archive_count/entries stay 0):\n 1) RSA: result \e sig^(*key2) mod (*key1), keys \e param_2/param_3 (\e provider+0x60/+0x68). Recovered plaintext length must \e\e 0x41 (65) .\n 2) Whirlpool: W(packetData[5..endOfEntries]) compared to plaintext[1..64] . plaintext[0] (magic byte) is NOT checked anywhere - any non-zero leading byte works (0x0a and 0x01 behave identically).\nOn success : archive_count(+0x10)\ecount, entries(+0x18)\ealloc. On ANY failure: returns with archive_count\e0, entries\eNULL (object still allocated). This count\e0 is what makes RequestGroupFromDisk trap at 0xb61ad0 for the first low-index request.
func=jag::Js5MasterIndex::Js5MasterIndex	func_addr=0x00b5ca60	kind=eol	insn_offset_from_entry=798	cu_index_from_entry=154	text=RSA-decrypted plaintext length MUST \e\e 0x41 (65). If not -> fall through to cleanup, return with archive_count(+0x10) left 0 (master index REJECTED). Wrong RSA modulus patch -> garbage length (~modulus size) -> reject here.
func=jag::Js5MasterIndex::Js5MasterIndex	func_addr=0x00b5ca60	kind=eol	insn_offset_from_entry=1194	cu_index_from_entry=230	text=Whirlpool over packetData[5 .. endOfEntries] \e archiveCount byte + entries table (count*0x50). RDI\edata+5, RSI\ebitLength\e(1+count*0x50)*8. Server must hash EXACTLY this range (excludes leading 5 bytes and trailing signature).
func=jag::Js5MasterIndex::Js5MasterIndex	func_addr=0x00b5ca60	kind=eol	insn_offset_from_entry=1285	cu_index_from_entry=242	text=Compare computed whirlpool[0..63] (R11) to plaintext[1..64] (RDI+1..). plaintext[0] (RSA block magic byte) is NEVER read/compared - no magic-byte check. Mismatch -> 0xb5e980 -> reject (archive_count left 0).
func=jag::Js5MasterIndex::Js5MasterIndex	func_addr=0x00b5ca60	kind=eol	insn_offset_from_entry=3793	cu_index_from_entry=789	text=ACCEPT: archive_count(+0x10)\ecount, entries(+0x18)\eallocated. Reached only after length\e\e65 AND whirlpool match. This is the ONLY writer of archive_count to non-zero.
func=jag::game::ConfigProvider::GetVarBitType	func_addr=0x00589c90	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::ConfigProvider::GetVarBitType. Checks enum field at this+0x3c \e\e 4, then virtual-dispatches through the VarBitType list pointer at this+0x230 (vtable+0x40). Same logical pattern across versions (enum check + virtual dispatch through member-ptr), but STRUCT OFFSETS DIFFER between builds - do not copy offsets across versions. Called from packet handlers, opcode handlers, and varbit checks.
