func=jag::PacketHandlers::IfSetplayerheadSnapshot	func_addr=0x001879f0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eIF_SETPLAYERHEAD_SNAPSHOT direction\eSERVER opcode\e150 size\e5\n\nPayload: 4-byte packed interface+component id; g1_add snapshot slot.\nSetComponentProperty(mgr, componentId, kind\e3, value\e(-2 - slot), extra\e0). The negative sentinel\n-2-slot is how a snapshot slot is encoded instead of a live player id.\nEvidence: same kind\e3 as IF_SETPLAYERHEAD  (which passes the live local player id\ninstead), and the identical -2-slot encoding appears in the kind\e5 sibling .\nResidual risk: see IF_SETPLAYERHEAD -- head-vs-model orientation follows the model-type enum\nordering, not a located consumer.
