func=jag::PacketHandlers::MessageQuickchatFriendchat	func_addr=0x001494c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt handler op\e0x21, size\e-1 (byte var-length). CATEGORY: Chat (CERTAIN). OPCODE NAME: UNKNOWN (canonical not verified).\nPAYLOAD: [u8 hasSeparateDisplayName][gjstr name][if\e\e1: gjstr displayName else copy name][gjstr message][u16 ?][u8,u8,u8 packed 32-bit msgId][u8 chatTypeIdx][u16 channelId]. Reads name+optional displayName+message via FUN_00ad80e0; builds 32-bit local_14c message id; chatTypeIdx indexes table DAT_015a4aa0 (stride 0xc, crown img id at +4, name-color/flag at +9).\nENGINE CALL CHAIN: jag::RelationshipManager::IsOnIgnoreList(Client+RELA[0xcfe], name) -> if ignored, drop. Recent-message dedup ring DAT_013942e0 (100 ints) prevents duplicate display. Builds '<img\e%d>' rank-crown prefixes via FUN_00146960. jag::ChatHistory::AddChat_hookable(Client+0x19408-area, type\e0x14, ...) then FUN_0019e140.\nEVIDENCE: (1) IsOnIgnoreList + crown img tags + dedup ring \e classic PUBLIC overhead/chatbox chat; (2) AddChat_hookable already-named (matches OFunctions.CHATHISTORY_ADDCHAT_HOOKABLE); (3) reference jag::packethandlers::Chat; (4) byte-var size consistent.\nHYPOTHESIS: public typed chat message (likely MESSAGE_PUBLIC), AddChat type 0x14. Canonical opcode name not verified -> left UNKNOWN.
