func=jag::LoginManager::LoginStepWaitingServerClientVarConfigData	func_addr=0x00183490	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=LoginStepWaitingServerClientVarConfigData (login state 0x104\e260) — reads the raw VarClient block bytes (TASK B "Part A"). NOTE: Jagex's beta symbol for this 0x104 handler is actually "LoginStepWaitingServerClientVar" (suffix swapped in this DB vs real symbols). Waits for svrClientVarLen (loginMgr+0x1c8) bytes, ReadBytes them, copies into the Packet at loginMgr+0x198 (size@+0x1a0, data@+0x1a8, pos@+0x1b0). Transitions to state 0x10e (LoginStepWaitingServerClientVar ) which parses the entries. See that function for the [flag][g2 id][value] entry format.
