func=jag::game::HeightMap::GetFineHeight	func_addr=0x005037c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::HeightMap::GetFineHeight - height sampling for an interpolated subtile position. Confirmed via existing namespace and behavioral match (height sampling). Sibling HeightMap methods (ApplyHillRotation, AddLocationHeightOffset, RemoveLocationHeightOffset, GetTileHeight, GetFineWaterDepth, GetHeightMap, GetWaterHeights) are not yet separately identified in this build - some may be inlined. Follow-up: cross-reference NPC/Location MainLogic sites that feed AABBs to HeightMap and look for callers computing 3-corner normals.
func=jag::graphics::GraphNode::AddChild	func_addr=0x0078a430	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::graphics::GraphNode::AddChild — adds param_2 (child GraphNode) to param_1 (parent GraphNode). VERIFIED OFFSETS (match engine OGraphNode):\n- param_2 + 0xFC |\e 0x47 — sets dirty/posChanged/hasBounds bits on child (FLAGS \e 0xFC)\n- param_2 + 0x130 \e param_1 — writes parent pointer in child (PARENT \e 0x130, not in engine)\n- param_1 + 0x138 \e children vector begin (CHILDREN \e 0x138)\n- param_1 + 0x140 \e children vector end\n- param_1 + 0x148 \e children vector capacity\n- param_1 + 0x158 \e inline children buffer ptr (cannot be freed)\nPush pattern: 1. If end < cap: write child to *end, end +\e 8. 2. Else: reallocate vector (double capacity), memcpy, free old (unless it equals +0x158 inline buffer).\nCalled when populating the scene-graph tree; Locations are added to their containing parent's graphNode via this. The MapSquare callsite uses MapSquare+0x8 (MapSquare's GraphNode pointer) as the parent — confirming MapSquare is Entity-derived with GRAPH_NODE \e 0x8.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::UpdateInvPartial	func_addr=0x001863e0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::PacketHandlers::UpdateInvPartial -- ServerProt UPDATE_INV_PARTIAL decoder (949-1 opcode 43,\nsize -2 varShort).\n\nHeader: g2 containerKey, g1 flags (bit0 keyFlag, bit1 hasObjVars).\nContainer \e InventoryManager::GetInventory(mgr, containerKey, flags&1), falling back to\nCreateInventory when absent -- the partial form preserves an existing container.\n\nThen, until the read cursor reaches *payloadLength, repeated slot records:\n  gSmart1or2  slotIndex\n  g2 (or g3 when the obj-count global DAT_0144460c >\e 0x3b5)  objId, wire \e objId + 1, 0 \e empty\n  amount: g1, and if that byte \e\e 0xFF then g4 -- OMITTED ENTIRELY when objId \e\e 0\n  varCount: g1, only when objId !\e 0 and flags & 0x02\n  vars: varCount x { g2 varId, g4 value } via jag::game::VarDomain::FindOrCreateEntry\nFinally pushes containerKey onto the 64-entry container-refresh ring (base +0xa8, counter +0xb0).\n\nEvidence: (1) matches docs/net/serverprot/inventory.md UPDATE_INV_PARTIAL field-for-field,\nincluding the amount-omitted-when-empty rule that distinguishes it from UPDATE_INV_FULL;\n(2) it is the run-to-end form (no slot count on the wire, slot index carried per record) whereas\nthe FULL decoder is count-prefixed and dense; (3) prot table size -2 matches the documented\nvarShort; (4) offset table records the 948-5 predecessor at 0x00184320, which the docs name\nUpdateInvPartial.\n\nDrift vs the 948-5 doc: objId is not unconditionally g2 -- a global threshold selects a 3-byte\nform. Worth re-checking whether the doc predates that widening.
