func=jag::PacketHandlers::IfSettargetparam	func_addr=0x00187f40	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eIF_SETTARGETPARAM direction\eSERVER opcode\e118 size\e10\n\nPayload: [0..1] g2_add toSlot (0xFFFF -> -1), [2..3] g2_add_LE fromSlot (0xFFFF -> -1),\n[4..5] g2LE targetParam, [6..9] g4 componentId.\nDecisive: calls jag::InterfaceManager::SetServerActiveProperties (0x00206470) on the interface\nmanager at client+0x19488 (INTERFACE_LIST in the engine offset table). The already-named IfSetevents\n(0x00187660) calls the same function with the same slot-range arguments but passes the packet's\nevent mask in R8D and a hardcoded -1 in R9D; this handler passes 0 for the event mask and a real\nvalue in R9D, plus the trailing flag 1 instead of 0. R9D is therefore the target parameter, and this\npacket sets it over a component slot range.
