func=jag::WorldLobbyData::GetHTTPURL	func_addr=0x001b2950	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Patcher target: MOV R8D, 0x50 (port 80 hardcoded for LIVE mode). The Project X patcher overwrites the 4-byte immediate at offset +2 with PROJECTX_HTTP_PORT. 948 pattern: 41 b8 50 00 00 00 74 (JZ follows). GetHTTPURL is NOT inlined into callers in 948 — this is the single site.
func=jag::WorldLobbyData::GetHTTPURL	func_addr=0x001b2950	kind=plate	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Setting prototype: eastl_fixed_string_256 * GetHTTPURL(eastl_fixed_string_256 * result, WorldLobbyData * this)
func=jag::WorldLobbyData::GetHTTPURL	func_addr=0x001b2950	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=147	cu_index_from_entry=33	text=Project X patcher target: the live-mode HTTP content port literal. This port is used when the ClientParameters TLS flag is clear and the server profile is the live/default one; the runtime patcher rewrites this immediate with the port from PROJECTX_HTTP_PORT so the client fetches JS5-over-HTTP content from the local server.\n\nHow the patcher locates it: by the pair of world-port base constants that this same basic block adds to the world id, taking the literal from its fixed position relative to them. It deliberately does NOT key on the surrounding opcode bytes, because register allocation around the literal differs between compilers, between builds, and between the two copies of this logic in this build.\n\nThis logic exists at MORE THAN ONE SITE in this build. The compiler also inlined the whole body of this function into jag::ClientCrashReportingDataProvider::GetAddress, which reaches the same WorldLobbyData through the Client. Both sites must be patched, or the crash-reporting path keeps reporting the unpatched port. Re-check the site count on every build and on every platform rather than assuming any particular shape.
func=jag::opcode::worldmap_disabletextsize	func_addr=0x003b8f70	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=CS2 opcode handler. Self-named via embedded literal CreateOpcodeError("worldmap_disabletextsize"). Setter mirror of worldmap_getdisabletextsize. Writes bool to byte field at +0x29c/+0x29d/+0x29e of worldmap object based on enum selector (0/1/2). Throws on invalid enum. Ported 948-2-2 (0x00269000) -> 948-5 (0x002691c0): confirmed by self-naming string + identical field offsets (+0x29c/+0x29d/+0x29e).
