func=jag::PacketHandlers::TelemetryGridAddGroup	func_addr=0x0011da00	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eTELEMETRY_GRID_ADD_GROUP direction\eSERVER opcode\e179 size\e5\n\nPayload: 4-byte scrambled group id (byte order 2,3,0,1 -- g4_alt3 shape); g1_inv insert index.\nBuilds an empty grid/group record on the stack via FUN_006c1ab0(tmp, groupId) and inserts it into\nthe telemetry grid manager at Client+0x193d8 via FUN_006c1f30(mgr, tmp, index), then frees the\ntemporary's four vectors.\nEvidence: the confirmed TELEMETRY_GRID_FULL  uses the identical pair -- FUN_006c1ab0 to\nconstruct and FUN_006c1f30(Client+0x193d8, grid, -1) to insert -- and operates on the same 0x68-byte\ngrid records that TELEMETRY_GRID_MOVE_ROW / MOVE_COLUMN / SET_ROW_PINNED / CLEAR_GRID_VALUE index.\nThe only difference here is that an explicit insert index is supplied instead of -1 (append), and no\nrow/column payload follows.
func=jag::InterfaceManager::LogicComponentListInner	func_addr=0x00245820	kind=eol	insn_offset_from_entry=7222	cu_index_from_entry=1599	text=LOCAL CONSUMER OF THE MOVEMENT RING -- peeks the NEWEST entry, i.e. MouseInputRecorder::moveRing[(moveRingWrite - 1) mod 200], after first testing moveRingWrite !\e moveRingRead and skipping the whole block when the ring is empty. The write \e\e 0 case is special-cased to the last slot. It does NOT advance either cursor. This is the interface/component logic obtaining the current cursor position. HAZARD for synthetic input: writing movement entries changes what this reads, so the movement ring is NOT a prot-private structure.
func=jag::game::Conversion::WorldDeltaToRenderAngle	func_addr=0x00a71700	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Render yaw from a world-space horizontal delta \e atan2(-deltaXEast, -deltaZNorth) in radians (the atan2(dx,dz) result is shifted by +/-PI, which negates both args). Same radians space as the FACE_DIRECTION override at entity+0x23c (JagexAngleToRadians). Called by the entity orientation/turn update FUN_004a4050 with (targetX-selfX, targetZ-selfZ). Server inverse to face (dx,dy) tiles: angle16384 \e round(atan2(-dx,-dy)*16384/(2*PI)) & 0x3FFF.
