func=jag::game::HintTrail::BuildFromPacket	func_addr=0x00163de0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=HINT_TRAIL (ServerProt, SERVER, opcode 29) payload builder, called from jag::PacketHandlers::HintTrail.\n\nparam_1 \e HintTrailList (Client + OClient.HINTTRAIL_LIST), param_3 \e slot byte, param_4 \e target id.\nSlots live at list+0x10, stride 8, 8 slots (list+0x50 is the next member and is passed on to the\nentity as its owner pointer).\n\nReads a run-length coord list off the packet (gSmart1or2s count, then two unsigned shorts as the\nbase tile, then signed byte deltas per step), walks one tile at a time between successive coords and\nappends a HintTrailPoint per tile into the entity's fixed_vector at +0x70/+0x78/+0x80. Each point\nstores world-fine X at +0x08 and Y at +0x10 as (tile * 512) + 256, with height at +0x0c seeded to\n-1.0f and filled from HeightMap::GetFineHeight once LinkMap::ReadTileFlags says the tile is loaded.\n\nThe slot entity is allocated lazily here at 0x14b0 bytes (vtable PTR_FUN_01417130) and is a\njag::game::Entity subclass, so OEntity fields (type, plane) apply to it. The LAST point in the\nvector is the hint's destination - that is what the map hint icon marks.
