func=jag::game::ClientError::ReportFatalError	func_addr=0x00cd5240	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::ClientError fatal-error reporter. Builds a human message ("Fatal error occured!" + optional prefix/JagException text from param_5), then if the GLOBAL reporter DAT_015beb98 has the default vtable (FUN_0047d5b0) and a live reporter object (DAT_015beb98[0x116] \e\e client+0x8b0), calls jag::game::ClientError::ReportError (FUN_006ef050) with flags\e7 to POST to nxtclienterror.ws. This is the C++ fatal/exception funnel (distinct from the OS-signal path). DAT_015beb98[0x116]*8 \e\e 0x8b0 \e\e the reporter sub-object offset. Hooking ReportError (0x006ef050) covers this path too.
