func=jag::PacketHandlers::PointlightAttenuationFalloff	func_addr=0x001e2b60	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\ePOINTLIGHT_ATTENUATION_FALLOFF direction\eSERVER opcode\e170 size\e4\n\nPayload: g2LE pointlight id (signed short, little-endian); g2_add value (BE, low byte -0x80).\n0xffff clears the override; otherwise light+0x158 \e value * DAT_00d677d4 (float) with the override\nflag at light+0x15c, applied to every scene light carrying the id.\nEvidence: the render-parameter builder FUN_006bae90 emits\n"params[8] \e light+0x15c ? light+0x158 : lightType+0x78" alongside "params[9] \e lightType+0x7c" --\ni.e. this is a per-instance override of the first of the light type's two adjacent attenuation\nfloats. It is a plain immediate scalar, distinct from the time-interpolated intensity scalar at\nlight+0x68 driven by POINTLIGHT_INTENSITYSCALE .
