func=jag::PacketHandlers::PointlightIntensityscale	func_addr=0x001e5110	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\ePOINTLIGHT_INTENSITYSCALE direction\eSERVER opcode\e191 size\e5\n\nPayload: g2_add duration (BE, low byte -0x80); g1_inv scale (0xff means 1.0); g2_add pointlight id\n(BE).\nDuration is divided by the client tick length (Client+0x4f8) and added to the current tick\n(Client+0x500) to give an expiry. For each matching scene light it sets light+0x70 \e light+0x68\n(animation start \e current value), light+0x6c \e scale * DAT_00d677d4 (target), light+0x74 \e end\ntick, light+0x78/+0x7c \e timestamps.\nEvidence: the per-frame light update FUN_006be940 interpolates light+0x68 from +0x70 toward +0x6c\nacross the +0x7c..+0x74 window, and light+0x68 is then multiplied into the light's final emitted\nintensity at light+0xec. A time-interpolated multiplier on intensity \e INTENSITYSCALE; the\nimmediate, non-animated float override at light+0x158 is ATTENUATION_FALLOFF .
