func=jag::game::LocationContainer::LocationContainer	func_addr=0x004956a0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=LocationContainer constructor. Object size 0x2F0 (all three construction sites in FUN_004e98e0 do `mov $0x2f0,%edi; call 0xcb98e0` at 0x4edd6f, 0x4ef270, 0x4ef3b8 immediately before calling here). The result is stored into the MapSquare loc-container grid at MapSquare+0xeb80 (store at 0x4eddf7), i.e. this is exactly the type jag::game::MapSquare::GetLocationContainerAt (0x004991a0) returns a pointer to.\n\nVerified head layout (from this ctor's own stores):\n  0x00 qword  vptr (base vtable 0x142ffa8 , derived vtable 0x141e658 )\n  0x08 qword  jag::graphics::GraphNode*  --  `mov %rcx,0x8(%rdi)`; the argument comes from\n              FUN_00158230 (a jag::graphics::GraphNode factory) at every call site (0x4edd58/0x4ef25c/0x4ef3a8).\n              Consumer proof: 0x00484cd1 loads it and calls jag::graphics::GraphNode::UpdateBounds on it.\n  0x10 byte   type/kind discriminator \e 9   --  `movb $0x9,0x10(%rdi)`.\n              Sibling classes use 4 () and 0xA (); read + switched at 0x4f2389\n              (`movzbl 0x10(%rdi),%edx; cmp $0x2 / $0x9 / $0x1`).\n  0x11 byte \e 6, 0x12 byte \e 6 (LOD, written by vtable[0xd0] stub FUN_00272bf0), 0x13 byte \e 0\n  0x14 dword \e 0\n  0x40 qword \e -1\n  0x48 qword + 0x50 qword  refcounted pair (IncRef at 0x494fc5)\n  0x58 qword  ptr (arg rsi)\n  0x60 qword  ptr (arg rdx)  -- SCALAR,  `mov %rdx,0x60(%rdi)`\n  0x68 byte \e 6  --  `movb $0x6,0x68(%rdi)`\n  0x69 byte \e 0  -- \n  0x6c dword  (arg r9d) -- ; this alone proves 0x68 cannot hold a qword\n  0x70/0x74/0x78/0x7c/0x80 dwords, 0x84 byte\n  0x88..0xf0 zeroed qwords: 0xb0/0xb8/0xc0, 0xc8/0xd0/0xd8, 0xe0/0xe8/0xf0 are the three\n              begin/end/capacity vector triples walked by FUN_00499210 and UpdateZoneFullFollows.\n  0xf8..0x2ef  SEVEN 0x48-byte dispatch slots (0xf8, 0x140, 0x188, 0x1d0, 0x218, 0x260, 0x2a8);\n              each slot holds a vector at slot+0x00 and a second vector at slot+0x28.\n              Slot index comes from the 5-entry byte table at 0x144462c\n              (0x495412 `lea (%r14,%r14,8),%r12; shl $0x3,%r12` \e idx*0x48).\n\nNEGATIVE RESULTS (checked deliberately):\n  - No eastl red-black tree exists anywhere in this object. An eastl rbtree header would self-link its\n    anchor (mpNodeLeft \e mpNodeRight \e &anchor) and keep a node count; nothing of the sort is emitted\n    here, and 0x8/0x10 are a GraphNode* and a byte respectively.\n  - There is no vector at 0x60/0x68. 0x68 is a byte and 0x6c is a dword, so no qword can live at 0x68.\n    The vector<shared_ptr<MapSquareLocation>> at +0x60/+0x68/+0x70 belongs to the *loc-change manager*\n    object at Client+0x19490 (see jag::game::ApplyLocChange ), a different class.
