func=jag::LoginManager::LoginStepWaitingConnectionOpened	func_addr=0x00184e40	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::LoginManager::LoginStepWaitingConnectionOpened - the world/lobby RECONNECT step (login sub-state 0xe). Reads WorldSwitcher (client+RELA[0xd01]); for loginType (LoginMgr+0x20)\e\e2 (WORLD) target\e*(WS+0x20), else (LOBBY) target\e*(WS+0x30). port \e (target+0x2c\e\e0) ? port1(target+0x28) : port2(target+0x2a). Calls game::ServerConnection::OpenConnection(conn, target+0x10 /*host string*/, port) which builds a fresh ClientStream to \\"host:port\\". PROOF that lobby<->world is a RECONNECT to the world's own host:port (separate socket), NOT socket reuse. The world and lobby can be separate servers on separate ports. RE rs2client.948-5.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::ClientSetvarcbitSmall	func_addr=0x00117290	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eCLIENT_SETVARCBIT_SMALL direction\eSERVER opcode\e54 size\e3\n\nPayload: g1s value (signed byte, raw); g2 varbit id (BE).\nEvidence: id is resolved through the varbit type table (default &DAT_01457030, else vftable+0x40\nlookup on the config provider) -- the same varbit resolution the confirmed VARBIT_SMALL\n performs. The value is then applied by FUN_00ada260, which reads the varbit's parent\nvar (type+8) and masks the value in using the varbit lsb/msb fields (+0x48/+0x4c), writing into\nthe CLIENT varc update manager (Client+0x19450). Varc domain (not PlayerVarDomain) + varbit\nmasking \e> CLIENT_SETVARCBIT; 1-byte value \e> SMALL.
