func=jag::PacketHandlers::PlayerInfo	func_addr=0x00169f80	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::PacketHandlers::PlayerInfo — ServerProt op22 (PLAYER_INFO / GPI), size -2 (varShort). Per-tick Global Player Info decode. Bit-packed via Packet::Bit::gBit (MSB-first); the gBit cursor lives in a 2-field stack pair {packetPtr, bitPos}, byte-aligned back to packet->position (+0x18) as (bitPos+7)>>3 after each block.\nFour NSN passes (need-second-notify parity split on PlayerInfoSlot.nsnFlag +0x27):\n 1. HIGH-RES pass A  — known high-res list, slots with nsnFlag\e\e0\n 2. HIGH-RES pass B  — known high-res list, slots with nsnFlag!\e0\n 3. LOW-RES  pass A  — known low-res  list, slots with nsnFlag!\e0\n 4. LOW-RES  pass B  — known low-res  list, slots with nsnFlag\e\e0\n(high-res and low-res use OPPOSITE parity ordering — the classic GPI cohort alternation.)\nEach pass, per slot in list order whose nsnFlag matches: if a run-skip is active, decrement and skip; else [1] hasUpdate. hasUpdate\e\e0 -> ReadStationary ([2] mode + [5/8/11] count) gives the run-length of following idle slots. hasUpdate\e\e1 -> high-res passes call GetHighResolutionPlayerPosition; low-res passes call GetLowResolutionPlayerPosition.\nAfter the 4 blocks: rotate flags for every slot (nsnFlag \e processedThisTick; processedThisTick \e 0) and rebuild the two known-lists (membership by playerEntity +0x38 !\e 0). Then byte-align and read the EXTENDED-INFO section: for each slot queued during the bit section (in queue/processing order — high-res first), skip the [u16 BE blockLength] (packet->position +\e 2) then PlayerEntity::ProcessExtendedInfo(entity, cycleCounter, packet). The appearance mask block is the carrier; its byte layout is a separate task.\nDispatch-only handler (bound at ProtEntry+0x28 via PlayerList::BindHandlers). VERIFIED 948-5.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::PlayerInfo	func_addr=0x00169f80	kind=plate	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\ePLAYER_INFO direction\eSERVER opcode\e45 size\e-2
func=jag::PacketHandlers::PlayerInfo	func_addr=0x00169f80	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=1242	cu_index_from_entry=286	text=END-OF-TICK ROTATE + REBUILD (per non-null slot 1..2047; slot 0 reserved). (1) reset both known-lists to empty; (2) for every slot: nsnFlag(+0x27)\eprocessedThisTick(+0x26); processedThisTick\e0; (3) re-add slot to HIGH-RES list if playerEntity(+0x38)!\e0 else LOW-RES list, in ascending slot-id order. INITIAL STATE (HandleAbsolutePlayerPositions ): local slot \e high-res, nsnFlag\e0; every other slot \e low-res, nsnFlag\e(seed moveSpeed\e\e0) \e> 1 for the standard moveSpeed-0 GPI-init seed. So at login all low-res slots are nsnFlag\e1 (processed first in low-res passA/block3).
func=jag::Js5ResourceProvider::RequestGroupFromDisk	func_addr=0x00b603f0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=CRASH SITE for JS5 startup SIGSEGV (fault PC \e 0xb61ad0). Reftable/index path: groupId\e\e0xffffffff.\nthis+0x25b8 \e Js5MasterIndex* (built in WorkerOnMessage case 10). Trap at 0xb61ad0 when masterIndex->archive_count(+0x10) <\e archiveId.\nROOT CAUSE (refined): the master index was REJECTED by the ctor (Js5MasterIndex ) - RSA-decrypted length !\e 65 OR whirlpool(body) !\e plaintext[1..64] - so archive_count is left 0 while the object is still stored non-null at this+0x25b8. The first low-index reftable request (e.g. archiveId\e2) then trips 0 <\e 2 -> UD2. (NOT a too-small archive-count byte, and NOT the RSA block magic byte, which is never checked.) Fix: RSA key patch must match the signer; whirlpool must cover packetData[5..endOfEntries].
