func=jag::game::WorldAreaTypeList::WorldAreaTypeList	func_addr=0x00614ca0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::WorldAreaTypeList::WorldAreaTypeList (base ConfigTypeList part; sets base vtable PTR_FUN_01420b50 + loader strategy @this+0x38/+0x7*8). The DERIVED object (0xb68 B, vtable PTR_FUN_01420580) is finished in ConfigProvider::EnsureTypeListsLoaded @the g83 slot (ConfigProvider+0x1e0, DAT_01692a44\e0x53): fromColour reverse hash_map @this+0x78 (0x20 buckets, key\eWorldAreaType+0x38 colour RGB24, generic eastl hash_map), base id->type map @this+0x48, per-map-square composite LRU rbtree @this+0xb28 (ulong key). Vtable slots: 0/1 dtor, 4\eCacheReset, 5\eLRU-trim, 8\eList(id)->shared_ptr. GetAreaColoursForMapSquare (colour grid) NOT yet located in 949 - see re-resources/docs/net/worldmap-worldarea-system.md sec 5.
func=jag::PlayerEntity::SetAppearanceAsPlayer	func_addr=0x00152d40	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::PlayerEntity::SetAppearanceAsPlayer(decoder) \e\e ref jag::PlayerEntityAppearanceDecoder::DecodeAppearanceAsPlayer (decode+apply merged). Decodes the APPEARANCE ext-info block of PLAYER_INFO (op22). param_1(decoder): flags@0, titleId@4(short), displayMode@8(int), name eastl::string, morphNpc, pn1, headIcon0, headIcon1, colourFlag(byte), colour0 colour1 colour2 colour3 skin(short), targetPlayerEntity, embedded Packet (data,pos), baseAppearanceDecoder.\n\nDELIVERY (ProcessExtendedInfo 0x0015e290): per queued slot PlayerInfo skips [u16 BE blockLen] (pos+\e2, value ignored) then reads mask (1-4 byte LE, expansion bits {0,13,22}); APPEARANCE \e mask bit3/0x08 (947 was bit2). Block \e [appLen \e gScrambledByte cipher3 \e readUByteSubtract \e (128-wireByte)] [payload appLen bytes \e gScrambledArrayBuffer cipher2 \e each byte readUByteAdd (clean \e wire-128), forward]. Cipher table  \e {3,2} FIXED. The un-scrambled payload is read raw below.\n\nPAYLOAD WIRE ORDER (clean, after un-scramble; all VERIFIED 948-5 vs authentic live capture, appLen\e67 'ProjectX101' full Imphide set):\n 1) flags \e g1. 0x01 FEMALE, 0x02 HAS_OBJ_OVERRIDES, 0x04 MORPH_AS_NPC, 0x08|0x10|0x20 renderSize\e((flags>>3)&7)+1, 0x40 HAS_TITLE, 0x80 TITLE_AFTER_NAME.\n 2) if flags&0x40: titleId \e gSmart1or2 (id , -1\enone).\n 3) if flags&0x02: objOverrides \e g1 count, then count x (g2 id + g1 value).\n 4) displayMode \e g1 ().\n 5) EQUIPMENT region \e PlayerEntityBaseAppearanceDecoder::DecodeBaseAppearanceAsPlayer (0x141b40); outer pos advances by region len at baseDecoder+0xbc. Per wear-slot (cache count, 16 in capture): g1 b0; b0\e\e0 -> empty; else g2 v\e(b0<<8)|b1: slot0 v\e\e0xffff -> OBJ-MORPH(gSmart2or4s+g1); v<0x800 -> bodyPart(id\ev-0x100); else worn item(id\ev-0x800). Then recolorMask\eg2 (per type0-slot customisation blocks if bits set); ARRAY1\e10x g1; ARRAY2\e10x g1; BAS\eg2 (-1\edefault).\n 6) name \e gStringCP1252ToUTF8 (RAW null-term CP1252 in the un-scrambled buffer; the +0x80 seen on the wire is the gScrambledArrayBuffer mode-2 transform, NOT a string encoding) -> .\n 7) headicon: pn1 \e g1 (). if flags&0x04(MORPH): morphNpc \e g2 (, 0xffff->-1), headIcon0\epn1, headIcon1\e-1. else: headIcon0 \e g1 (), headIcon1 \e g1 (, 0xff->-1), morphNpc\e0.\n 8) colourFlag \e g1 (). if !\e0: colour0..3 \e 4x g2 (/0x3c/0x3e/0x40), skin \e g1 (). if \e\e0: all 5 \e -1 (cache default colours).\nNo combat level / no explicit idle/walk anims in this block (anims derive from BAS id).
