func=jag::PacketHandlers::UpdateInvFull	func_addr=0x001ab890	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::PacketHandlers::UpdateInvFull -- ServerProt UPDATE_INV_FULL decoder (949-1 opcode 8,\nsize -2 varShort).\n\nHeader: g2 containerKey, g1 flags (bit0 keyFlag, bit1 hasObjVars), g2 slotCount.\nContainer \e InventoryManager::CreateInventory(mgr, containerKey, flags&1) unconditionally -- the\nfull form discards any prior container with the same key.\n\nThen exactly slotCount dense records for slots 0..slotCount-1 (no slot index on the wire):\n  g2 (or g3 when the obj-count global DAT_0144460c >\e 0x3b5)  objId, wire \e objId + 1\n  amount: g1, and if that byte \e\e 0xFF then g4 -- present for EVERY slot, including empty ones\n  varCount: g1 whenever flags & 0x02 -- likewise present for every slot\n  vars: varCount x { g2 varId, g4 value } via jag::game::VarDomain::FindOrCreateEntry\nFinally pushes containerKey onto the 64-entry container-refresh ring (base +0xa8, counter +0xb0).\n\nEvidence: (1) matches docs/net/serverprot/inventory.md UPDATE_INV_FULL field-for-field, including\nthe count-prefixed dense layout and the unconditional amount byte that distinguish it from\nUPDATE_INV_PARTIAL; (2) CreateInventory rather than GetInventory-then-create is the documented\nFULL behaviour; (3) prot table size -2 matches the documented varShort; (4) offset table records\nthe 948-5 predecessor at 0x001a8d30, which the docs name UpdateInvFull.\n\npayloadLength (RDX) is passed by the dispatcher but unread here -- the loop is bounded by the\non-wire slotCount. Confirmed at the entry disassembly: RDX is never touched.\n\nDrift vs the 948-5 doc: objId is not unconditionally g2 -- a global threshold selects a 3-byte\nform. Worth re-checking whether the doc predates that widening.
