func=jag::PacketHandlers::TelemetryGridSetRowPinned	func_addr=0x000ed8d0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eTELEMETRY_GRID_SET_ROW_PINNED direction\eSERVER opcode\e224 size\e3\n\nPayload: g1_inv row index; g1_sub pinned flag; g1_inv grid index.\nWrites grid[gridIdx].pinned[rowIdx] \e pinned ? rowIdx : -1 (int vector at grid+0x38, telemetry\ngrid manager Client+0x193d8, grid stride 0x68).\nEvidence: grid+0x38 is the per-row pin vector -- FUN_006c1840 (the row-move helper used by\nTELEMETRY_GRID_MOVE_ROW) relocates it in lockstep with the row-data vector at grid+0x50, and\nTELEMETRY_GRID_MOVE_ROW re-normalises exactly this vector (element \e its own index) after a move.\nStoring the index itself vs -1 is the pin/unpin encoding.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::UpdateFriendchatChannelFull	func_addr=0x0019aa00	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=949 op63 UPDATE_FRIENDCHAT_CHANNEL_FULL (var_short) — CAPTURE-VERIFIED against 37B sample (resolves prior "op67"/"do not trust" HYPOTHESIS: this IS the FC-channel-full decoder; op63 per prot_names_949-1.json + byte-exact decode). Wire: gStr ownerName; g1 ownerHasPrevName [+gStr prevName if 1]; gStr channelName; i8 kickRank(+0x3c); memberCountEncoded byte (b<0x80 -> count\eb-1, b\e\e0 \e channel closed; else g2 short +0x7fff); per member {gStr name; g1 hasPrevName [+gStr prevName if 1]; g2 world; i8 rank; gStr worldName}. Sample: "Yehp" 00 "Ironman Btw" 07 02 "Yehp" 00 0450 07 "Lobby 5". See docs/949-1/net/social/friends-chat.md
