func=jag::PacketHandlers::VarpLarge	func_addr=0x00117490	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eVARP_LARGE direction\eSERVER opcode\e78 size\e6\n\nPayload: [0..3] g4_alt3 value (b1<<24|b0<<16|b3<<8|b2), [4..5] g2 varpId (BE).\nResolves the type via ConfigProvider::GetVarType with the VARPLAYER type list , then\ncalls jag::game::PlayerVarDomain::SetVarValueFromServer on client+0x19b40 (PLAYER_VAR_DOMAIN in the\nengine offset table). Non-bit variant; the bit variant is VarbitLarge.
func=jag::packethandlers::Friends::UPDATE_FRIENDLIST	func_addr=0x001a3410	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=949 op3 UPDATE_FRIENDLIST / FriendStatus (var_short) — CAPTURE-VERIFIED against 1057B/63-friend sample (supersedes stale "op26" numbering; op3 per prot_names_949-1.json + byte-exact decode). Layout unchanged from 948 (schema P). Per friend record (loop while pos<len): g1 warnMessage(0 normal,1 name-change); gStr displayName; gStr previousName; g2 worldId(0\eoffline); g1 fcRank; g1 flags(bit0\ereferredByYou, bit1\ereferredByThem); if worldId>0 {gStr worldName; g1 platform; g4 worldFlags}; gStr notes. Stores stride 0x78, sets RelMgr+0x10\e2. See docs/949-1/net/social/friends.md
func=jag::packethandlers::Social::op130_RELATIONSHIP_DELTA_UNCONFIRMED	func_addr=0x001dc8b0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt op130 (0x82), VarByte. IDENTITY UNCONFIRMED — do NOT trust the "UPDATE_IGNORELIST" name in any prior label/CSV.\n\nThis is NOT the rev-947 UPDATE_IGNORELIST (a loop of {flag-byte + 3 CP1252 strings} ignore records). Decompile shows a SINGLE relationship/friend entry built from a 64-bit flag mask:\n  - gT_ulong flagMask\n  - if mask\e\e0: clears all fields (a remove/empty-entry form)\n  - else ~48 conditionally-gated fields keyed by individual mask bits 0..0x2f (smart readers, coord triples, packed-uint->3 floats color/vector, trailing g2)\n  - allocates a 0x1e0-byte entry, stores to *(RelationshipManager+0x98), frees old, sets dirty flag +0xa0 \e 1.\n\nPer-friend RELATIONSHIP DELTA packet (single entry, flag-gated), redesigned in 948. CRITICAL: needs a live lobby capture with a friended/ignored account to nail the flag-bit -> field mapping. LEAVE AS UNKNOWN until then.
func=jag::InterfaceManager::SendIfButtonD	func_addr=0x00252eb0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=HYPOTHESIS / NAME WARNING: this function is currently called SendIfButtonD but it is far larger\nthan a single prot emitter and it is the per-tick INPUT PROCESSING pass -- it reads\nMouseInputRecorder::clickRing cursors and builds the per-tick input-event view over BOTH\nKeyboardInputRecorder rings (keyRing and charRing) as (begin,end) pointer pairs. The IF_BUTTOND\nemitter is probably just one inlined branch of it. Do not trust the current name; re-derive it\nbefore relying on it.
func=jag::InterfaceManager::SendIfButtonD	func_addr=0x00252eb0	kind=eol	insn_offset_from_entry=4340	cu_index_from_entry=1014	text=Builds the per-tick input-event VIEW over KeyboardInputRecorder::keyRing: reads keyRingRead and keyRingWrite, and when they differ stores a (begin,end) POINTER pair into the view object. The pointers address the recorder's live ring records directly, they are not copies. The server-bound key stage later walks exactly such a (begin,end) pair with a 0x20 record stride and filters on KeyEvent::repeat. The char-ring equivalent is built a few instructions later into a second pointer pair in the same view object.
func=jag::InterfaceManager::SendIfButtonD	func_addr=0x00252eb0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=17539	cu_index_from_entry=3730	text=ClientProt IF_BUTTOND op25 size\e18 (949 form; VERIFIED vs 5 live captures, iface 1430 action-bar drag). Payload byte layout (offset:len field \e write fn):\n 0:2  TO.item    pT<short> BE          (server readShort)\n 2:3  TO.slot    3B [v>>8, v>>16, v]   (middle medium, NO std helper; -1 in captures)\n 5:3  FROM.slot  3B [v>>16, v>>8, v]   \e writeMedium BE (server readMedium; -1 in captures)\n 8:2  FROM.item  writeShortAddLittle   (server readUShortAddLittle) [lo-0x80, hi]\n10:4  TO.hash    pT<int> BE            (server readInt)   \e (iface<<16)|comp\n14:4  FROM.hash  p4_alt2 \e writeIntMiddle [B1,B0,B3,B2] (server readUIntMiddle)\nSample1 body: ff ff | ff ff ff | ff ff ff | 7f ff | 05 96 00 5c | 00 42 05 96 -> toItem\e-1 toSlot\e-1 fromSlot\e-1 fromItem\e-1 toHash\e(1430<<16)|0x5c fromHash\e(1430<<16)|0x42.
func=jag::InterfaceManager::SendIfButtonD	func_addr=0x00252eb0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=18172	cu_index_from_entry=3877	text=ClientProt IF_BUTTOND_LEGACY op153 size\e16 (pre-949 form; selected when DAT_0144460c<0x3b5). Payload order: TO.hash FUN_00136ef0(p4 BE) , TO.slot writeShort+item... (legacy 16B: hash4 + slot2 + item2 per triple). Not used by 949 client - the 18B op25 form above is what a 949 client sends. Kept for completeness.
func=jag::game::DoOpLoc4	func_addr=0x00163520	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=DoAction OBJECT_4, id 5 (MiniMenu action object DAT_01448540: static init FUN_000af050 sets base+0x20 id\e5, base+0x24 kind\e3; ctor FUN_00078b4e installs this sender at base+0x18). Emits ClientProt op 91, fixed size 9, via descriptor DAT_01683f90. This is the sender the engine offset table recorded as 0x0 (missing) prior to 2026-07; the table had the whole loc family shifted one slot, labelling this address OBJECT_3.
