func=jag::ClientProt::SendQueuedEvents	func_addr=0x00189e10	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::SendQueuedEvents \e\e emitter of ClientProt STORE_SERVERPERM_VARCS (op105, varShort, ProtEntry DAT_01683eb0; RegisterAll index 0x69 size -2). CONFIRMED (prior 'EVENT_NATIVE/UI event stream' hypothesis was WRONG). Flushes the map of CHANGED serverpermanent var_client values (param_1+0x78 hashmap merged into the +0xa8 vector of 0x28-byte {int key, typed value, byte typeTag} records), throttled ~1/sec (param_1+0xa0 +\e 1000ms), capped 0x5dd\e1501B/packet, resumes across packets via index param_1+0xc0. Server replies op200 StoreServerpermVarcsAck (1:1). Payload after varShort len:\n  [0] u8 completeFlag: 1 \e all remaining records fit in this packet (final chunk); 0 \e 1501B cap hit, more follow in the next op105.\n  then repeated per record: pT<short> varcId (2B BE) ; value encoded by the varc's value-domain (int domain \e pT<int> 4B BE; long/string domains would differ - none seen).\n  No count, no terminator; records run to end of payload.\nVERIFIED vs 2 live bodies: 01 |1b35\e1 |0b67\e.. |0b68\e.. |0d89\e.. -> varcIds 6965/2919/2920/3465 (all toplevel_v2 *_savestate_* / *_serverperm). Emitter called from ConnectionManager::LoginProtocolHandler.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::TelemetryGridFull	func_addr=0x0011db10	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=op199 REBUILD_NORMAL_MULTI_SCENE (ServerProt opcode 199, varShort). Sibling of WORLDENTITY_ADD(, single) and REBUILD_WORLDENTITY(, patch matrix cells). CLEARS then REBUILDS the WorldList (eastl::vector<RebuildSceneEntry>, stride 0x68, max 8) at Client+0x193d8, the same composite/world-entity list. This packet only POPULATES descriptors; it does NOT set the scene base coord or trigger the build. The scene base (\eplayer chunk - centerOffset) and the actual build are driven by op81 REBUILD_NORMAL() + op78 zones.\n\nWIRE FORMAT (all multi-byte \e big-endian g4 unless noted; DAT_01050dc0\e\e0x3020100 is the LE-host check, always true on x86 so the bswap branch is always taken):\n[g1 sceneCount]\nper scene:\n  [g4 sceneKey]                      -> RebuildSceneEntry::Reset(entry, sceneKey)\n  [g1 srcCount]\n  srcCount x [g4 srcKey]             -> srcKeys vector (also creates matrix row + level\e-1)\n  [g1 destCount]\n  destCount x [g4 destKey]           -> destKeys vector (appends 0x80000000 placeholder to every matrix row)\n  if srcCount>0:                      MATRIX (row-major [src][dest]):\n    srcCount x {\n      [g1 level]                     (SIGNED byte) -> levels[src]\n      destCount x {\n        [g1 flag]\n        flag!\e0 ? [g4 value] : (no bytes, cell stays 0x80000000)\n      }\n    }\n  game::WorldList::InsertOrReplace(Client+0x193d8, entry, -1)\n\nvalue g4 \e packed source-chunk descriptor (standard RS dynamic-region template, CONFIRMED by jag::game::ClientCompositeData::DecodeFromRegionData & DecodeFromWorldArea in reference): rotation\e(v>>1)&3, srcChunkY\e(v>>3)&0x7FF, srcChunkX\e(v>>14)&0x3FF, plane\e(v>>24)&3. 0x80000000 (high bit set) \e empty cell / no source (reference's older sentinel was 0xFFFFFFFF). NOT an XTEA key - op199 carries NO XTEA; encrypted map squares are loaded from cache. Captured 133B payload decodes exactly (sceneCount\e4; scene1 src{7,4,6}->dest{1,2,4} values 0x87/0x251c/0x0c2c all at chunkX\e0 \e template area).
