func=jag::opcode::INV_GETVAR	func_addr=0x002eff10	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=CS2 opcode INV_GETVAR(inv, slot, varId): reads a per-item-stack variable.\nPops 3 ints from the script int-stack: arg0\einventory id, arg1\eslot, arg2\evarId\n(a varbitobject; e.g. 30212 \e augmented-item XP). GetInventory(mgr, inv, 1).\n\nOBJ-VAR STORAGE (the answer to "where item vars live"):\n  inventory+0x28 \e EASTL vector<VarContainerSparse> { begin@+0x28, end@+0x30, cap@+0x38 }\n  per-slot stride 0x38. Bounds check: slot < (end-begin)/0x38.\n  entry \e *(inv+0x28) + slot*0x38  -> a jag::game::VarContainerSparse\n  (a sparse var container \e hash keyed by BASE var id, value \e packed varbit storage).\n  result \e entry->vtable[0x20](entry, varType)   // VarContainerSparse::GetVarBitValue\narg2 (varId) is first resolved to a VarBitType via the config provider\n(runner-relative global; the field+0x3c\e\e4 branch resolves obj-scope varbits).\n\nEngine cross-ref: OInventory.INVENTORY_ITEMS\e0x10, OInventory.OBJ_VAR_DOMAINS\e0x28;\nObjVarDomain in inventories/Inventory.kt reimplements GetVarBitValue (VarbitType ->\nbaseVar -> hash lookup -> shift/mask). Item XP \e varbitobject 30212.\nEvidence: sole cluster handler reading inv+0x28 (siblings INV_GETNUM/INV_GETOBJ/INV_TOTAL\nread inv+0x10); 3-arg signature matches CS2 INV_GETVAR(inv, slot, varObjId).
