func=jag::InterfaceManager::IfButtonXInner	func_addr=0x003ea170	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=NOT the official jag::InterfaceManager::IfButtonX. This inner takes 7 args (extra trailing char 'defer'); the official IfButtonX(shared_ptr<Component>, uint, int, int, char const*) is the 6-arg wrapper at 0x003f0010, which guards on component vtbl+0x68 and then calls here. It is also not IfButtonXSend, whose first param is a shared_ptr<ServerConnection>. Keep the Inner name.
func=jag::InterfaceManager::IfButtonXInner	func_addr=0x003ea170	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=1632	cu_index_from_entry=356	text=IfButtonXInner else-branch (component has text: lVar13 !\e 0) emits ClientProt op102 (var_byte). Descriptor 0x01683ee0, registered id 102 size -1. Wire: [op102][size:u8][p1 (textLen+8)][2 bytes param_4 low,high \e u16 LE sub][p1 param_5 (button slot/index)][jagString component text via FUN_00acd630][p4 BE param_3 (packed interface:component hash)][p1_inverse -(component field +0x29)]. Fires when an interface component that carries text is actioned (e.g. chat input submit) — live capture shows op102 (var_byte ~15B) sent in-world alongside the op71 PM. This is the IF_BUTTON variant that transmits the component's text. (Plain IF_BUTTON1..10 use the descriptor table (&PTR_DAT_0141d4e0)[idx] in the sibling branch.)
