func=jag::PacketHandlers::VarpSmall	func_addr=0x00117550	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eVARP_SMALL direction\eSERVER opcode\e95 size\e3\n\nPayload: g1s value (signed byte); g2 varp id.\nEvidence: calls jag::game::PlayerVarDomain::SetVarValueFromServer -- the plain-var sibling of\nSetVarBitValueFromServer used by the confirmed VARBIT_SMALL . Player var domain (not\nthe client varc manager at Client+0x19450) \e> VARP_*; 1-byte value \e> SMALL.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::HintArrow	func_addr=0x00185f90	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=HINT_ARROW (ServerProt, SERVER, opcode 83, size 14).\n\nThe hint arrow/icon list is a SEPARATE container from the hint TRAIL list and sits 8 bytes before it\non the Client: MOV RSI,[RDI] ; MOV RBP,[RSI + 0x19478]  (trail list is +0x19480).\n\nThat container holds three parallel 8-slot arrays, indexed by the packet's slot \e firstByte >> 5:\n  +0x10 + slot*8    arrow entity pointer   (non-null \e this slot is live)\n  +0x50 + slot*8    arrow pointer entity   (the on-screen pointer)\n  +0x90 + slot*0x2c descriptor POD, written directly by this handler\n\nDescriptor fields (uint indices off +0x90 + slot*0x2c):\n  +0x00 slot, +0x04 kind (2 \e coordinate hint; 1/10 \e entity hint), +0x10 target entity index\n  +0x1c float fine X   \e tileX * 0x200 + subtile   (first  gT_unsigned_short)\n  +0x20 float height   \e packet byte * 8\n  +0x24 float fine Y   \e tileY * 0x200 + subtile   (second gT_unsigned_short)\n\nReading the descriptor is the cheap, safe way to get where a hint points: one deref off the Client\nand a fixed-stride index, with no scene-graph walk and no shared_ptr chasing.
