func=jag::PacketHandlers::LogoutTransfer	func_addr=0x001aa230	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt op213 SWITCH_WORLD handler. Wire (ORDER MATTERS, differs from op212): [g2 worldId] [gStr host (CP1252, NUL-terminated)] [g2 port1] [g2 port2] [g1 flag]. Builds WorldLobbyData{worldId@+8,host@+0x10,port1@+0x28,port2@+0x2a,isWorld/+0x2c\e1} into WorldSwitcher+0x18(shared_ptr)/+0x20(raw) \e the WORLD-node slot, sets WorldSwitcher+0x58\e(flag\e\e1), then Client::SetMainState(0x25). State 0x25 -> LoginManager::OnMainStateTransition -> StartWorldLogin -> opens a NEW socket to host:port. Because the built WorldLobbyData has +0x2c\e1, LoginStepWaitingConnectionOpened uses port2(+0x2a) for the connect. THIS is the server packet that points the client at a world server and triggers the lobby->world reconnect. RE rs2client.948-5.
