func=jag::game::VarType::DecodeType	func_addr=0x006b8b10	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::VarType::DecodeType -- generic per-entry cache decoder shared by ALL var domains (VarPlayerType/varp, the CLIENT domain aka "var_client"/varc, Clan, ClanSetting, World, PlayerGroup). There is NO separate "VarClientType" class: ConfigProvider::GetVarType (0x005addf0) dispatches by domain tag to one of 7 ConfigTypeList<VarType> instances (configProvider+0x1f8.. +0x228); the CLIENT domain (archive 62 / var_client) list sits at configProvider+0x208. VarBitType (0x004c64e0) is the one domain with its own dedicated class (needs bit-range fields).\n\nOpcode table (byte opcode read via g1, loop terminates on opcode 0, default case returns shared success sentinel DAT_015df0b8 -- same sentinel as VarBitType::DecodeType):\n  op 3   : g1 -> ScriptVarType::GetByID(byte)  \e> baseType (+0x40)      [base value type: INT/LONG/STRING/COORDFINE/...]\n  op 4   : g1 raw byte                          \e> lifetime (+0x48)     [jag::game::VarLifetime enumArray index -- values PERMANENT/TEMPORARY/SERVERPERMANENT confirmed via librs2client.so symbols. THIS IS THE SERVERPERM/PERSISTENCE CLASSIFIER.]\n  op 5   : g1 raw byte                          \e> transmitLevel (+0x49)[jag::game::VarTransmitLevel enumArray index -- includes at least NEVER]\n  op 0x6e: g2 BE (via FUN_0018f870)             \e> field_0x6e_opcode (+0x4c) [HYPOTHESIS: possibly clientCode/script-binding id, unconfirmed]\n  op 7   : no operand, byte :\e 0                \e> flag_opcode7 (+0x50)  [HYPOTHESIS: stable across both builds, purpose unconfirmed]\n  op 8   : no operand, byte :\e 1                \e> flag_opcode8 (+0x51)  [HYPOTHESIS: NEW in 948-5, not present in librs2client.so reference; unconfirmed]\n\nNo opcode reads a per-var default VALUE. GetDefaultValue (librs2client.so 0x001c1700) just virtual-dispatches through the resolved baseType's (ScriptVarType) own vtable+0x10 -- defaults are generic per base-type (e.g. 0 for INTEGER, "" for STRING), not stored per-var in this decode table. Cross-verified against jag::game::VarBitType::DecodeType (0x004c64e0) for shape/pattern; librs2client.so VarType::DecodeType  confirms opcode numbers 3/4/5/0x6e/7 and the VarLifetime/VarTransmitLevel/ScriptVarType symbol names (severely outdated build -- used for pattern/name confirmation only, not byte layout).
