func=jag::Packet::gScrambledArrayBuffer	func_addr=0x0027e1c0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::Packet::gScrambledArrayBuffer — bulk array analog of jag::Packet::gScrambledByte (0x0047f840). Reads ONE transform-selector byte from the cipher cursor at packet+0x28 (post-incremented; points at an in-binary const table, NOT the wire), then copies `length` data bytes from packet+0x10 (pos at +0x18) into dest+0x10 using that mode:\n  mode 0 \e forward, raw           (readFully)\n  mode 1 \e reverse, raw           (readFully, byte-reversed)\n  mode 2 \e forward, byte-0x80     (per-byte readUByteAdd; clean \e wire-128)\n  mode 3 \e reverse, byte-0x80     (per-byte readUByteAdd, byte-reversed)\nUsed by ProcessExtendedInfo for the APPEARANCE payload (cipher table \e APPEARANCE_EXTINFO_SCRAMBLE_CIPHER  \e {0x03,0x02}; entry[1]\e2 -> appearance payload is mode 2). VERIFIED 948-5 against authentic live PLAYER_INFO capture (payload bytes are clean+0x80 on the wire).
