func=jag::PacketHandlers::IfClosesub	func_addr=0x00188340	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=OFFICIAL_PROT_NAME\eIF_CLOSESUB direction\eSERVER opcode\e107 size\e4\n\nPayload: g4 packed interface+component id (BE).\nLooks the id up in the open-sub-interface hash map on the interface manager (Client+<sub mgr>,\nbuckets at +0xf8, modulus at +0x100); when found and not already in state 2, it takes a ref on the\nentry and calls FUN_00244cc0(mgr, &entry, 1, 0) to tear the sub-interface down, then clears the\npending-open slots at mgr+0x158 / +0x160 and drops the refs.\nA single packed component id whose only effect is removing the matching open sub-interface is\nIF_CLOSESUB.
func=jag::game::PlayerVarDomain::SetVarBitValue	func_addr=0x004fcee0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Official name from re-resources/symbols/parsed_functions.txt: jag::game::PlayerVarDomain::SetVarBitValue(jag::shared_ptr<jag::game::VarBitType> const&, int, bool*). Confirmed: 4 args exactly; writes *arg4 \e true/false depending on whether the value fits the bit range, splices bits via VarBitType lsb (+0x48) / msb (+0x4c), reads through vtable slot +0x10 (GetVarValue) and writes through slot +0x18 (SetVarValue). Vtable slot +0x28 of the PlayerVarDomain vtable at 0x0141b968; the pointer occurs in exactly one vtable, so it is not shared/ICF-folded with ClientVarDomain or EntityVarDomain.
