func=eastl::rbtree::next	func_addr=0x00cb2e90	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=eastl::rbtree::next — standard EASTL/STL red-black tree successor iteration. Node layout (offsets in bytes): +0x00 pointer to left child, +0x08 pointer to right child (NEXT in iteration order), +0x10 pointer to parent. Node payload starts after +0x18 (varies by node type). Algorithm: if node has a right child (+0x08 !\e null), descend to its leftmost node and return it; otherwise walk up via parent (+0x10) until arriving from a left child (came-from-right keeps walking up), returning that parent (or the node itself if the root is hit). Used heavily to iterate static-location / world trees with a sentinel node.
func=jag::InterfaceManager::GetParentLayer	func_addr=0x003f0cd0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Reads component +0x0e as an index into the interface's static component array\n(base \e iface->+0x08->+0x08, stride 0x18, same formula as InterfaceList::GetStaticComponent).\n0xffff \e no parent layer. +0x0e is a parent component id, not a type discriminator.
