func=jag::ClientCrashReportingDataProvider::GetAddress	func_addr=0x00317520	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=291	cu_index_from_entry=68	text=Project X patcher target: a SECOND occurrence of the live-mode HTTP content port literal in this build. The compiler inlined the entire body of jag::WorldLobbyData::GetHTTPURL here, so this is the same logic as that standalone function rather than a distinct one.\n\nUsed when the ClientParameters TLS flag is clear and the server profile is the live/default one; the runtime patcher must rewrite this immediate with the port from PROJECTX_HTTP_PORT here as well.\n\nHow the patcher locates it: by the pair of world-port base constants this block adds to the world id, not by the surrounding opcode bytes. Those bytes differ from the standalone function because this inlined copy is register-allocated differently, so a byte signature written for that site will not match here.\n\nSkipping this site leaves the crash-reporting data provider reporting the unpatched port.
func=jag::game::MapSquare::MapSquare	func_addr=0x004dadd0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::MapSquare constructor. Object stride 0x10d80 (caller IMUL R14,R10,0x10d80 ).\n\nField evidence (949-4 linux-x86_64):\n  +0x40  qword \e -1 sentinel (param_1[8] \e 0xffffffffffffffff). NOT mapsquareX.\n  +0x5c  int  \e arg4 (mapsquare X)\n  +0x60  int  \e arg5 (mapsquare Y)\n  +0x68  qword \e compositeData shared_ptr CONTROL block (arg6[0]), LOCK INC [ctrl+8]\n  +0x70  qword \e compositeData OBJECT (arg6[1]); tested for null by\n         MapSquare::GetLocationContainerAt  -> chunkSize \e compositeData ? 8 : 16,\n         so COMPOSITE_DATA and CHUNK_SIZE_FLAG are the same field.\n  +0xa8  byte (not a shared_ptr control word)\n  +0xb0  qword zero-init, never assigned compositeData\n  +0x1e8/+0x1ec   second copy of X/Y (PointLightGrid AABB + "PointLightGrid (%i,%i)")\n  +0xece0/+0xece4 third copy of X/Y\n  +0xeb80/+0xeb88/+0xeb90  locationContainers vector begin/end/cap\n\nX-vs-Y resolution (three independent lines, all put arg4\eX at +0x5c):\n  1. teardown  loads [+0x5c]->ESI, [+0x60]->EDX, matching the (X\eRSI, Y\eRDX)\n     argument order of World::GetMapSquare  and GetLocationContainerAt .\n  2. light-grid AABB stored (minA,minB,maxA,maxB) at +0x70..+0x7c from (arg4,arg5)\n     \e the (minX,minY,maxX,maxY) convention.\n  3. "PointLightGrid (%i,%i)" formats (arg4, arg5).
func=jag::game::PlayerVarDomain::SetVarValue	func_addr=0x004fd140	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Official name from re-resources/symbols/parsed_functions.txt: jag::game::PlayerVarDomain::SetVarValue(jag::shared_ptr<jag::game::VarType> const&, jag::game::VarValue const&). Confirmed: vtable slot +0x18 of the PlayerVarDomain vtable at 0x0141b968 (object at Client+0x19b40 \e OClient.PLAYER_VAR_DOMAIN); SetVarBitValue (0x004fc780, the definitive 4-arg official match) calls this slot with varBitType->baseVar (shared_ptr<VarType>) and a VarValue, and GetVarValue (slot +0x10, 0x004f08a0) reads the same map at this+0x1c0c8 that this writes. Takes 3 args only (RDI/RSI/RDX; RCX is clobbered before use), so it is NOT SetVarBitValue. WARNING: previously named setBit / engine OFunctions.PLAYERVARDOMAIN_SETBIT - that name is a misnomer, this sets a whole var, not a bit.
